gress; independent factual review requested. No source qualification or acceptance claim added.\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-28T11:43:35Z\",\n  \"review\": \"ACCEPT by independent read-only reviewer /root/review_pr302 at exact head 5d2932f0a90516343c52bb36531a93f29aa921cd and base b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff; cumulative diff SHA-256 9b9d6494eded840a13a27306e2c94e94ede6dfd3aaf5facffae935eaf1a10a22; no findings\",\n  \"review_diff_sha256\": \"9b9d6494eded840a13a27306e2c94e94ede6dfd3aaf5facffae935eaf1a10a22\",\n  \"last_updated\": \"2026-10-28T16:19:38Z\",\n  \"independent_review\": {\n    \"disposition\": \"ACCEPT\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"/root/review_pr302\",\n    \"base\": \"b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212\",\n    \"head\": \"11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492\",\n    \"diff_sha256\": \"2ab25de0645cb96bc4f874f35e4f327817f93a29216c12ef463ad380192b6513\",\n    \"findings\": 0,\n    \"tests_run\": false,\n    \"confirmed_at\": \"2026-10-28T14:05:17Z\"\n  },\n  \"diff_sha256\": \"2ab25de0645cb96bc4f874f35e4f327817f93a29216c12ef463ad380192b6513\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T13:34:00Z\",\n  \"review_correction\": {\n    \"prior_review_head\": \"484cfbf290e1c28c4c0bf233b697651a854e8b76\",\n    \"disposition\": \"CHANGES_REQUIRED\",\n    \"finding\": \"checkpoint reported main Node22/24 still running though both passed; source-PR row named PR300 prior head\",\n    \"new_head\": \"96cc7dcb3235ef8d12f7e12025dd24e8e4ef92b5\",\n    \"diff_sha256\": \"01418bd9d9b39f5de0c98eb513d3b627525e4dfa149cdf03109a5dba12ddedbf\",\n    \"review\": \"PENDING\"\n  },\n  \"previous_claim_head\": \"96cc7dcb3235ef8d12f7e12025dd24e8e4ef92b5\",\n  \"exact_head_checks\": {\n    \"node22\": \"success\",\n    \"node24\": \"success\",\n    \"javascript_typescript\": \"success\",\n    \"codeql\": \"success\",\n    \"linux_x86_64\": \"success\",\n    \"entire\": \"failure: no reviewer approved trail 15\"\n  }\n}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"--- readiness ---\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 11666)\nTotal output lines: 105\n\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 16:16 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`. Exact-head CI run [40720824591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824591) passed the Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices; the Linux packaging/reproducibility job was still running at observation time. CodeQL run [40720824319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824319) passed. The CI jobs completed `sync-version --check` and the requirements checker successfully on this source. These results qualify the source revision only; they do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Release PRs:** PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is merged at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`, included in current main. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is based on `145d464` at exact head `662d084ade9b7c724cc2268cacc60d1ac7a1a19e`; its follow-up preserves sibling staged and worktree state during nested-workspace restore. An independent source reviewer ACCEPTed that exact diff (SHA-256 `61f4e40bc135152ffa003c82bdc31fc15703542b5bd9ba3b67f7b6b1edae1cb2`). TypeScript `--noEmit` and `git diff --check` pass locally; no local suite was run under the active SUITE claim. Exact-head Node 22/24 tests, JS/TS analysis, CodeQL, and Entire gates are running.\n\nPR [#307](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/307) is based on `145d464` at `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`. Its clean-checkout build-identity correction has an independent ACCEPT review for the exact diff (SHA-256 `c0c7b8be14de2cf1aab3246b2f34596ba4aae30c2d527c1afbe93e1ce0105295`); JS/TS and CodeQL pass, while Node 22/24 and Entire remain pending. PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) contains this readiness record. Its branch has been updated to include current main; exact checks for that updated head are pending. PRs [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) and [#306](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/306) are explicitly v1.1 scope and are not part of the v1.0.0 merge path.\n\n**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. The newly pushed #302 head must complete its exact checks before that evidence is refreshed. No exact-RC qualification has started. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\nIssue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, live provider and standalone checks, cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source CI is mostly complete on `145d464`, and #302/#307 have independent source review, but exact PR checks remain pending and no accepted RC exists. Publication authorization remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n\nThe checkpoint below (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC) is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source revision, CI, PR heads, and release-gate state.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\n\n**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after a partial source read and did not run tests as part of that review. A separate owner-authored PR update records `tsc --noEmit` and 53/53 targeted restore tests, and advises a second review of `checkpoint.ts` because of its size. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\n\n**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\n\n**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 13:34:51 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n\n**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check pa…6666 tokens truncated…ract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n425:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\n435:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n453:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n467:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n477:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n491:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n517:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n538:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n553:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n564:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\n577:- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n657:| `REQ-PRV-003` | implemented | Standalone behavior has scripted tests but no qualifying live standalone evidence (HIST-08). | Installed RC; standalone matrix | Provider qualification operator | Run `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 for supported server profiles and archive sanitized receipts. |\n663:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\n666:| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\n683:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n684:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n693:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n712:### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\n724:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n728:| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"--- checks ---\nCodeQL\tpass\t4s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122945931346\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724869271/job/122945305243\t\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t1m12s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724869215/job/122945305983\t\nEntire Gates\tpending\t0\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code/trails/17\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724869271/job/122945304727\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped\nCodeQL\tpass\t5s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122945808375\t\nEntire Gates\tpending\t0\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/15/changes/nexus-code/15\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724835391/job/122945184529\t\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t1m11s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724835381/job/122945184452\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724835391/job/122945184299\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped\n{\"baseRefOid\":\"145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08\",\"headRefOid\":\"49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"BLOCKED\",\"reviews\":[],\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40724869271/job/122945305243\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-28T16:19:46Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-28T16:20:58Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/