{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:52.525Z","ordinal":454499,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a7632c41-98b7-4d50-aba7-286e1639502a","process_id":"6360","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'RC10|cross.runner.*pass|REQ-REL-114.*pass|provider.*RC10|RC10.*provider' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0 /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews 2>/dev/null | head -100; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 log --oneline --decorate -3; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 rev-parse HEAD;"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'RC10|cross.runner.*pass|REQ-REL-114.*pass|provider.*RC10|RC10.*provider' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0 /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews 2>/dev/null | head -100; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 log --oneline --decorate -3; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 rev-parse HEAD;"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:39:**Runtime identity dogfooding defect:** The user-reported RC8 behavior in which a Claude-specific skill led the model to describe Nexus as Claude Code has a source fix in merged PR [#273](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/273), integrated at `d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1` (PR merge commit `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`). The fixed system prompt states Nexus Code is the host and is appended after workspace skills; activated skills are also prefaced with `Host application: Nexus Code`. `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` reproduces a Claude model plus Claude-specific skill and verifies both boundaries. That test passed 1/1 in an isolated exact-main `b293b44` snapshot; PR #273's Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed, and exact-main CI also passed. The public RC10 tag (`16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`) predates the PR merge, so this fix still needs verification in the successor RC.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Disposition:** Engineering convergence remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. No RC is accepted and no stable release is published. Public RC10 remains the latest release; the repository target is the GitHub installer (npm publication is inapplicable per operator decision). Continue source remediation and exact-head review/CI, then build and qualify a successor RC only after pre-RC gates and PR #305's restart fix pass; keep all installed-RC gates bound to that exact artifact.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:67:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**RC10 E2 limits:** The archive still does not demonstrate a successful ordinary `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 to RC10, successful provenance-attestation verification, power-loss recovery, or an explicit staging-directory-cleanup assertion. The recorded updater process-death recovery is not a power-loss test. E2 acceptance remains open.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:81:**RC10 E2 limits:** The archive still does not demonstrate a successful ordinary `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 to RC10, successful provenance-attestation verification, power-loss recovery, or an explicit staging-directory-cleanup assertion. The recorded updater process-death recovery is not a power-loss test. E2 acceptance remains open.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:91:**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7ddce16a900d2da9def27d53722243bf4df2de07`, merging PR #284 atop PR #283 and earlier RC10 fixes. Post-merge CI [40593091251](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091251) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke jobs passed. CodeQL [40593091302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091302) also passed. On the refreshed readiness worktree, requirements enforcement passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and version synchronization confirms every component remains `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:95:**RC10 E2 evidence:** PR [#283](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/283) reports 20/20 fresh-install, doctor and Node-preflight cells: eight positive cells across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24, plus twelve negative preflight cells for absent Node or Node 12/20. However, independent review of merged head `71a4218` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED, and I confirmed the evidence archive is incomplete: 21 of 34 `SHA256SUMS` entries are missing, including all listed per-cell logs; `prepared-images.json` contains cell/image/id but not the distro and Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation. Treat the matrix as a recorded result, not independently accepted E2 evidence, until the archive and claims are corrected and reviewed. The single Ubuntu 22.04/Node 22 lifecycle script re-runs the installer for alpha.2→RC10, rollback, reinstall and repair; it does not exercise `nexus upgrade` or the separate self-test-failure, crash-recovery and backup-restore acceptance rows. Other lifecycle cases and platforms remain open. All evidence applies only to installed RC10.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:97:**PR #284 lifecycle follow-up:** PR [#284](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/284) added RC10 checksum-tamper, failed-self-test, backup-restore and updater-process-crash scripts and logs, then merged at `7ddce16a` despite an independent CHANGES_REQUIRED review. Its exact-head CI run [40586513330](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40586513330) passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL. The independent review found the updated checksum index still has 21 missing files out of 45; the earlier lifecycle path still does not test successful `nexus upgrade`; the `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` bypass is not clearly disclosed; and the process-crash script does not verify the claimed staging cleanup. The merged code therefore does not close the E2 archive or lifecycle evidence gaps. Its process-death recovery result explicitly does not test power loss. The post-merge main CI and CodeQL runs subsequently passed on `7ddce16a`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:107:**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, merging PR #279 after #278 and #277. Post-merge CI [40566591904](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591904) is running Node 22 and Node 24 on that exact SHA; CodeQL [40566591883](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591883) passed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL also passed on parent `cf05322` (runs [40561348972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348972) and [40561348985](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348985)). Source requirements and RC10 version-sync checks passed on `cf05322` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification). These are source-gate results, not installed-RC acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:111:**Other source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) corrected the configured-hook race and retention error-accounting findings left by #277. It merged at `fc582c6` after exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent read-only review passed. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) merged at `cf05322` as exact head `d617937`; its checks passed and independent evidence review accepted the sanitized ChatGPT receipts. That provider evidence covers the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row only. Open PR [#280](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/280) addresses configured state-directory recovery; Node 22/24 are running, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass. Open PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) records RC10 cross-runner reproducibility; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass, while Node 22/24 are running. These PRs do not establish the remaining provider/standalone matrix or release acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:113:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:127:**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:136:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`, integrating PRs [#269](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/269) and [#270](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/270) after #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505143) and CodeQL [40521505001](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505001) both passed on `3b7af5d`; CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests, security gates, packaging, reproducibility, package smoke, and installer smoke. PR #269 merge-commit CI [40519862728](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40519862728) passed on `f059770`. These runs establish CI for their exact commits, not the RC10 release gates.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:160:Five targeted synthetic installed-RC10 cancellation rechecks at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 completed with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remained valid and unresolved; this targeted recheck did not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are preserved in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). Human terminal acceptance remained 0/15. This historical record is retained from the PR #264 merge history.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:178:**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `d2442b0e0aa143191ab5ae478bc243ecce97861e`, which integrates PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266). Post-merge CI [40461301453](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40461301453) and CodeQL [40461301693](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40461301693) both completed successfully. PR #266 exact-head CI, including Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests/package and reproducibility, and CodeQL passed before merge. The source and its local regressions are integrated; this does not qualify the already-published RC10 artifact.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:180:**Current release PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) is open at `97e3f72e4a5fe8676a0a30ea9f6e023147ad73a5` on current base `d2442b0`; CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed and exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) is still running. PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) remains remotely at `bda6714ff885f2fd4fef736b84ca7005a9cddbdf`, based on the previous `303ea32` source. Its earlier CI and CodeQL passed on that older head. A local readiness candidate has been refreshed to `d2442b0`; requirement enforcement (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), RC10 version synchronization, and diff hygiene pass on the refreshed candidate. Independent review asked that the old 05:54 snapshot be clearly superseded; this checkpoint does so. The refreshed candidate still needs final-base review, owner push, and exact-head hosted checks.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:184:**Disposition:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC10 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains gated on all required qualification and independent acceptance. The 05:54 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source, PR #266 integration, current PR checks, and release-gate status by this checkpoint.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:192:**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:194:**Remaining exact-RC and release gates:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) archives RC10 scripted observations and keeps the manual matrix separate; its remote head is `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on a stale base, with all reported exact-head checks successful. Its manual worksheet is blank. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) still lacks custodian acceptance; the sealed public manifest alone is not private custody acceptance, and no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone qualification, full installed-RC provider coverage, exact-RC cross-runner checks, the manual matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published; publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:218:**RC10 artifact boundary:** The latest published prerelease is [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not current main. Its Linux archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Previously completed RC10 artifact, installation, provenance and cross-runner checks apply only to that immutable artifact. Scripted terminal coverage remains partial; the required manual real-terminal matrix is 0/15. No exact-RC acceptance is established. Further source changes require constructing and qualifying a new candidate.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:220:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:224:**Disposition:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC10 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated on all mandatory qualification and independent acceptance. The user-selected distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:331:**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the signature as unverified (`bad_email`); it is not verified-signature provenance. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; both results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:345:**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the signature as unverified (`bad_email`); it is not verified-signature provenance. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; both results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:359:**RC and qualification:** Signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` still resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive digest is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; those results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:371:**RC7 qualification evidence:** Signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` remains the latest published candidate, resolving to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; its Linux archive digest remains `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. Cross-runner reproducibility passed for RC7 only (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)); ChatGPT provider verification passed 3/3 on the installed RC7 using `gpt-6-luna`. A fresh provider-status check on the Ubuntu desktop at 01:54 UTC found ChatGPT connected and OpenRouter disconnected. RC7 evidence does not qualify a later candidate or establish acceptance.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:381:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:515:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:535:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:716:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027T174805Z.json:75:    \"This establishes only the ChatGPT sign-in provider verification for this exact RC10 artifact and run.\",\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/revie