u 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:95:**RC10 E2 evidence:** PR [#283](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/283) reports 20/20 fresh-install, doctor and Node-preflight cells: eight positive cells across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24, plus twelve negative preflight cells for absent Node or Node 12/20. However, independent review of merged head `71a4218` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED, and I confirmed the evidence archive is incomplete: 21 of 34 `SHA256SUMS` entries are missing, including all listed per-cell logs; `prepared-images.json` contains cell/image/id but not the distro and Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation. Treat the matrix as a recorded result, not independently accepted E2 evidence, until the archive and claims are corrected and reviewed. The single Ubuntu 22.04/Node 22 lifecycle script re-runs the installer for alpha.2→RC10, rollback, reinstall and repair; it does not exercise `nexus upgrade` or the separate self-test-failure, crash-recovery and backup-restore acce…7413 tokens truncated…9b8ff69cc5b91a40331f07c009f792afb63b5c04a995be4b10d00  s5_cancel_late_rc10_trial2.screens.txt\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/SHA256SUMS:268:213aafaceee0b8e2cb8ad5487deb195362de60c14436e5d1b643cfdc03613f75  s5_cancel_late_rc10_trial3.notes.txt\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/SHA256SUMS:269:8547f113376ee96f32a50de3e975c89b79a88aafc23e316bb8fcac5d8c6b25eb  s5_cancel_late_rc10_trial3.r