rix or release acceptance.\n113:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n127:**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n170:**Candidate and gates:** The latest public release remains prerel