quire a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\n57:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n93:**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\n111:**Other source PRs:** PR [#279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/279) corrected the configured-hook race and retention error-accounting findings left by #277. It merged at `fc582c6` after exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent read-only review passed. PR [#278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/278) merged at `cf05322` as exact head `d617937`; its checks passed and independent evidence review accepted the sanitized ChatGPT receipts. That provider evidence covers the ChatGPT verify-on-RC row only. Open PR [#280](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/280) addresses configured state-directory recovery; Node 22/24 are running, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass. Open PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) records RC10 cross-runner reproducibility; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pass, while Node 22/24 are running. These PRs do not establish the remaining provider/standalone matrix or release acceptance.\n113:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n127:**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n170:**Candidate and gates:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The required real-terminal matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence does not replace operator evidence. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no recorded custodian acceptance; no private payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, exact-current-RC provider/standalone and cross-runner qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization is granted but gated. The distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n194:**Remaining exact-RC and release gates:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) archives RC10 scripted observations and keeps the manual matrix separate; its remote head is `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on a stale base, with all reported exact-head checks successful. Its manual worksheet is blank. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) still lacks custodian acceptance; the sealed public manifest alone is not private custody acceptance, and no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone qualification, full installed-RC provider coverage, exact-RC cross-runner checks, the manual matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is publish…3130 tokens truncated…tial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 22:55 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7ddce16a900d2da9def27d53722243bf4df2de07`, merging PR #284 atop PR #283 and earlier RC10 fixes. Post-merge CI [40593091251](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091251) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke jobs passed. CodeQL [40593091302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091302) also passed. On the refreshed readiness worktree, requirements enforcement passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and version synchronization confirms every component remains `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\n\n**RC10 E2 evidence:** PR [#283](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/283) reports 20/20 fresh-install, doctor and Node-preflight cells: eight positive cells across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24, plus twelve negative preflight cells for absent Node or Node 12/20. However, independent review of merged head `71a4218` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED, and I confirmed the evidence archive is incomplete: 21 of 34 `SHA256SUMS` entries are missing, including all listed per-cell logs; `prepared-images.json` contains cell/image/id but not the distro and Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation. Treat the matrix as a recorded result, not independently accepted E2 evidence, until the archive and claims are corrected and reviewed. The single Ubuntu 22.04/Node 22 lifecycle script re-runs the installer for alpha.2→RC10, rollback, reinstall and repair; it does not exercise `nexus upgrade` or the separate self-test-failure, crash-recovery and backup-restore acceptance rows. Other lifecycle cases and platforms remain open. All evidence applies only to installed RC10.\n\n**PR #284 lifecycle follow-up:** PR [#284](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/284) added RC10 checksum-tamper, failed-self-test, backup-restore and updater-process-crash scripts and logs, then merged at `7ddce16a` despite an independent CHANGES_REQUIRED review. Its exact-head CI run [40586513330](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40586513330) passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL. The independent review found the updated checksum index still has 21 missing files out of 45; the earlier lifecycle path still does not test successful `nexus upgrade`; the `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` bypass is not clearly disclosed; and the process-crash script does not verify the claimed staging cleanup. The merged code therefore does not close the E2 archive or lifecycle evidence gaps. Its process-death recovery result explicitly does not test power loss. The post-merge main CI and CodeQL runs subsequently passed on `7ddce16a`.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** Its remote head remains `eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da` on the older base `fc582c66`; its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks all passed on that older candidate. The refreshed local readiness candidate `a3bb9e59e56e08de66ea5b7eaf682ce408b2e57f` includes current main `7ddce16a` and received independent ACCEPT from `rc5_candidate_review` against that exact base. Exact-main CI and CodeQL are green, but the refreshed candidate has not been pushed and therefore has no exact-head hosted checks. No merge is claimed.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 19:22 and earlier checkpoints below remain historical snapshots and are superseded for current source, evidence, PR, CI and acceptance status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 19:22 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, merging PR #279 after #278 and #277. Post-merge CI [40566591904](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591904) is running Node 22 and Node 24 on that exact SHA; CodeQL [40566591883](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591883) passed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL also passed on parent `cf05322` (runs [40561348972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348972) and [40561348985](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40561348985)). Source requirements and RC10 version-sync checks passed on `cf05322` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification). These are source-gate results, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** At 19:22 UTC, its remote head was `eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da`, based on `main@fc582c66`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed on this exact head; Node 22 and Node 24 were still running. The preceding head `9c153d9` had not completed Node 22/24 at the last observation; its JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed. No independent review is recorded on `eac6cdb`. This checkpoint update advances PR #268 again; its resulting head requires exact-head checks and independent review before merge.\n\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/SHA256SUMS\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md\n/ho