{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:24:04.293Z","ordinal":454513,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-32408b20-2d6b-4a8f-8f01-9b172a45a6ae","process_id":"86799","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md; cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md; cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/cross-runner/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# RC10 cross-runner reproducibility\n\nRequirement `REQ-REL-114` / acceptance `ACC-SUP-08`: **PASS** for the exact published `v1.0.0-rc.10` artifact.\n\n- Workflow: https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40433818126\n- Workflow source: `main` at `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`\n- RC tag object: `0e99eeb7268ec798d4859f01279c9db8b1ce42f6`\n- RC source commit: `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`\n- Both Ubuntu 22.04 and Ubuntu 24.04 builders completed with pinned Node 22.22.1/npm 10.9.4 and Rust 1.95.0.\n- The comparison job passed and matched both runner outputs to each other and to all six published artifacts.\n- Evidence artifact SHA-256: `f393db75f06cc9675b34941c8d5e42cb7de0f01892cc2f8e64a48c9998d4fcc7`.\n\nThe retained `repro-evidence.json` records tag, tree, lockfiles, toolchain, builder images, package script identity, and the SHA-256 for `SHA256SUMS`, notices, compatibility metadata, installer, archive, and SBOM. This is one passed exact-RC reproducibility gate; it does not establish overall product acceptance or stable-release readiness.\n# RC10 OpenRouter provider verification\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the three provider verification checks performed against the exact installed RC10 artifact. This does not by itself establish provider live-task acceptance; see `../openrouter-live-task/README.md`.\n\n- Candidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source commit `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Installed RC10 reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`).\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Result time: `2026-10-27T02:27:10.627Z`.\n- Passed checks: streamed completion, tool call, and tool-result round trip.\n- Three provider receipts are preserved in `openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`; each records the exact model and provider-reported cost `$0`.\n- Verification JSON and receipt hashes: `3b14fdc568ca9daa6f10582e090bbab447ab230a4aae42d24dac95166374e88e` and `de74a7052f03a63faddacc2dc8bb1cd0288328d633ed203ceecd4d3e0737d9e1`.\n\nThese records cover the provider verification path only. The synthetic task and its failed attempts are separately documented, and all held-out, long-task, fault-injection, terminal, cross-runner, independent acceptance, and stable-release gates remain outside this result.\n# RC10 OpenRouter live task\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the small live-task portion of provider E5, based on the final synthetic task below. Earlier attempts are retained as failures and are not counted as passes.\n\n## Candidate and environment\n\n- Candidate: signed `v1.0.0-rc.10`, tag target `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Published Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`.\n- Installed binary: `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`); it reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` during independent validation.\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Workspace: fresh synthetic repository under `/tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-js-v2-20261027/workspace`; no user project, held-out content, corpus, or private validator was used.\n- Baseline commit: `d3cfb387f62ca7ff20b4ed5a4bd8e90ee871cb41`.\n- Task run: 2026-10-27, 7 model requests, 36.215 seconds, provider-reported cost `$0`; the exact model is recorded in each receipt.\n\n## Accepted attempt\n\n`attempt-js-ascii/` contains the raw JSON result, stderr, inference receipts, flight log, baseline identity and hashes, final deliverable, unchanged test, and independent validation transcript.\n\nThe configured verifier was `node --test tests/slug.test.mjs`. Nexus reported `COMPLETED`, `PASSED`, and `isDeliverableBound: true`, with `unverifiedChangesPending: false`. The verifier executed one test case covering ASCII lowercasing, delimiter collapsing, non-ASCII handling, and trimming. Independent validation reran that verifier and added three assertions (`İ`, emoji separation, and whitespace-only input); all passed. Only `src/slug.mjs` was modified in the task workspace.\n\n## Failed attempts retained\n\n- `attempt-unsupported-verifier/`: the original Python run used unsupported unittest discovery syntax. Nexus failed closed with `UNVERIFIED` / `VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN`; it is not acceptance evidence.\n- `attempt-python-verifier-unbound/`: a supported Python verifier executed and passed its four tests, but Nexus did not bind the declared deliverable (`REGRESSION_FREE`, `isDeliverableBound: false`). Independent validation also found that Unicode-wide lowercasing violated the ASCII-only objective. This is a product/evaluator failure, not a pass.\n- The Python binding fix is tracked separately and has not been accepted; the independent reviewer requested a conservative correction for ambiguous Python `from package import name` syntax.\n\n## Scope limits\n\nThis evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in [`../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`](../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl) and [`../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json`](../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":49663}},"started_at_ms":1793204644292,"completed_at_ms":1793204644292}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:24:05.520Z","ordinal":454514,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18353-6e90-7f22-a3fc-dc07505857dd","call_id":"call_64138b12e31e4acba5d9751dac9031ac","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# RC10 cross-runner reproducibility\n\nRequirement `REQ-REL-114` / acceptance `ACC-SUP-08`: **PASS** for the exact published `v1.0.0-rc.10` artifact.\n\n- Workflow: https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40433818126\n- Workflow source: `main` at `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`\n- RC tag object: `0e99eeb7268ec798d4859f01279c9db8b1ce42f6`\n- RC source commit: `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`\n- Both Ubuntu 22.04 and Ubuntu 24.04 builders completed with pinned Node 22.22.1/npm 10.9.4 and Rust 1.95.0.\n- The comparison job passed and matched both runner outputs to each other and to all six published artifacts.\n- Evidence artifact SHA-256: `f393db75f06cc9675b34941c8d5e42cb7de0f01892cc2f8e64a48c9998d4fcc7`.\n\nThe retained `repro-evidence.json` records tag, tree, lockfiles, toolchain, builder images, package script identity, and the SHA-256 for `SHA256SUMS`, notices, compatibility metadata, installer, archive, and SBOM. This is one passed exact-RC reproducibility gate; it does not establish overall product acceptance or stable-release readiness.\n# RC10 OpenRouter provider verification\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the three provider verification checks performed against the exact installed RC10 artifact. This does not by itself establish provider live-task acceptance; see `../openrouter-live-task/README.md`.\n\n- Candidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source commit `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Installed RC10 reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`).\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Result time: `2026-10-27T02:27:10.627Z`.\n- Passed checks: streamed completion, tool call, and tool-result round trip.\n- Three provider receipts are preserved in `openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`; each records the exact model and provider-reported cost `$0`.\n- Verification JSON and receipt hashes: `3b14fdc568ca9daa6f10582e090bbab447ab230a4aae42d24dac95166374e88e` and `de74a7052f03a63faddacc2dc8bb1cd0288328d633ed203ceecd4d3e0737d9e1`.\n\nThese records cover the provider verification path only. The synthetic task and its failed attempts are separately documented, and all held-out, long-task, fault-injection, terminal, cross-runner, independent acceptance, and stable-release gates remain outside this result.\n# RC10 OpenRouter live task\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the small live-task portion of provider E5, based on the final synthetic task below. Earlier attempts are retained as failures and are not counted as passes.\n\n## Candidate and environment\n\n- Candidate: signed `v1.0.0-rc.10`, tag target `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Published Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`.\n- Installed binary: `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`); it reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` during independent validation.\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Workspace: fresh synthetic repository under `/tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-js-v2-20261027/workspace`; no user project, held-out content, corpus, or private validator was used.\n- Baseline commit: `d3cfb387f62ca7ff20b4ed5a4bd8e90ee871cb41`.\n- Task run: 2026-10-27, 7 model requests, 36.215 seconds, provider-reported cost `$0`; the exact model is recorded in each receipt.\n\n## Accepted attempt\n\n`attempt-js-ascii/` contains the raw JSON result, stderr, inference receipts, flight log, baseline identity and hashes, final deliverable, unchanged test, and independent validation transcript.\n\nThe configured verifier was `node --test tests/slug.test.mjs`. Nexus reported `COMPLETED`, `PASSED`, and `isDeliverableBound: true`, with `unverifiedChangesPending: false`. The verifier executed one test case covering ASCII lowercasing, delimiter collapsing, non-ASCII handling, and trimming. Independent validation reran that verifier and added three assertions (`İ`, emoji separation, and whitespace-only input); all passed. Only `src/slug.mjs` was modified in the task workspace.\n\n## Failed attempts retained\n\n- `attempt-unsupported-verifier/`: the original Python run used unsupported unittest discovery syntax. Nexus failed closed with `UNVERIFIED` / `VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN`; it is not acceptance evidence.\n- `attempt-python-verifier-unbound/`: a supported Python verifier executed and passed its four tests, but Nexus did not bind the declared deliverable (`REGRESSION_FREE`, `isDeliverableBound: false`). Independent validation also found that Unicode-wide lowercasing violated the ASCII-only objective. This is a product/evaluator failure, not a pass.\n- The Python binding fix is tracked separately and has not been accepted; the independent reviewer requested a conservative correction for ambiguous Python `from package import name` syntax.\n\n## Scope limits\n\nThis evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in [`../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`](../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl) and [`../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json`](../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json).\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793204645.520366}},"metadata":{"client_authored":fa