{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:30:00.744Z","ordinal":454763,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae22303215881a086d0b54f799df9bc","usage":{"input_tokens":152966,"cached_input_tokens":151808,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":510,"reasoning_output_tokens":348,"total_tokens":153476},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":30126207,"cached_input_tokens":29729920,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":115194,"reasoning_output_tokens":63797,"total_tokens":30241401},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8401883064,"cached_input_tokens":8312260736,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":23887171,"reasoning_output_tokens":13773984,"total_tokens":8425770235}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:30:02.363Z","ordinal":454764,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-19a77e25-acca-4dae-a4b6-0e6eb44a4a07","process_id":"16479","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'Entire Gates|entire gate|trail|independent reviewer|reviewer' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md .github 2>/dev/null | head -80; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/rulesets/25340146 --jq '.rules[] | select(.type==\"required_status_checks\") | .parameters.required_status_checks[] | [.context,.integration_id] | @tsv'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'Entire Gates|entire gate|trail|independent reviewer|reviewer' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md .github 2>/dev/null | head -80; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/rulesets/25340146 --jq '.rules[] | select(.type==\"required_status_checks\") | .parameters.required_status_checks[] | [.context,.integration_id] | @tsv'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:110:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:115:- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:16:| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:286:The reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:288:The reviewer receives:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:296:The reviewer performs:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ntest-matrix (22)\t15368\ntest-matrix (24)\t15368\nlinux-x86_64\t15368\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":418126123}},"started_at_ms":1793205001941,"completed_at_ms":1793205002360}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:30:04.252Z","ordinal":454765,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18358-e7dc-77b3-972f-0cd3fca9dac7","call_id":"call_ffaf06c34dcc42b6bf62243640aa47b5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:110:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:115:- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:16:| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:286:The reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:288:The reviewer receives:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:296:The reviewer performs:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ntest-matrix (22)\t15368\ntest-matrix (24)\t15368\nlinux-x86_64\t15368\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793205004.2523031}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
