et is the GitHub installer (npm publication is inapplicable per operator decision). Continue source remediation and exact-head review/CI, then build and qualify a successor RC only after pre-RC gates and PR #305's restart fix pass; keep all installed-RC gates bound to that exact artifact.\n\nThe 07:55 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, CI, PR, and qualification state is superseded by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 07:55 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.ts` reduced to 12,818 bytes; runner revalidation, execution, and persistence are separated from `operation_runner.ts` (14,931 bytes). Runner decomposition and bounded revalidation/runner diagnostics were integrated through PR [#287](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/287); TDD evidence diagnostics landed through PR [#295](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/295), and scheduler observer diagnostics through PR [#296](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/296). PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297), now merged, adds regression coverage for the TDD diagnostic paths. The capability split and scheduler extraction were integrated through PRs [#286](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/286) and [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285), respectively. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293) added operator guidance for `DecisionRejected` and is merged with its Node 22/24, Linux, and CodeQL checks successful. These source changes are implemented on current `main`.\n\n**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\n\n**Operator configuration scope:** `~/.config/nexus/config.json` is the operator-owned structured configuration entry point for `operationPolicy`, with schema validation, bounded file size, symlink rejection, and environment/config/default precedence documented in `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`. The schema is intentionally limited to that policy today; this record does not claim every runtime default is configurable or that a repository-level config can override operator policy.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n\n   170\t  maxWaitMs: number;\n   171\t  /** Executions restarted after their outcome was lost; matches the UNKNOWN inference replay bound. */\n   172\t  unknownResumeBudget: number;\n   173\t  /** Runs of one unit before the scheduler stops retrying it. */\n   174\t  maxRunsPerUnit: number;\n   175\t  /** Floor between WAITING wake-ups. */\n   176\t  minWaitMs: number;\n   177\t}\n   178\t\n   179\texport const DEFAULT_OPERATION_POLICY: OperationPolicy = {\n   180\t  maxWaitMs: 12 * 60 * 60_000,\n   181\t  unknownResumeBudget: 2,\n   182\t  maxRunsPerUnit: 25,\n   183\t  minWaitMs: 1_000,\n   184\t};\n   185\t\n   186\t/** One unit's worktree/branch in an isolated operation. */\n   187\texport interface OperationGitUnit {\n   188\t  branch: string;\n   189\t  worktree: string;\n   190\t  /** Integration tip the branch was created from. */\n     1\t/**\n     2\t * Drives a ConvergenceScheduler: executes the unit it picks, feeds resource observations back into the registry,\n     3\t * waits durably when nothing is runnable, revalidates resources on wake, and persists after every transition so a\n     4\t * restarted process continues from the same decision point.\n     5\t */\n     6\timport { credentialStorageHome, storedCredentialFor } from \"../client.js\";\n     7\timport type { HarnessConfig } from \"../types.js\";\n     8\timport { realRecoveryClock, type RecoveryClock } from \"./provider_recovery.js\";\n     9\timport { ConvergenceScheduler, type Decision, type DurableOperationState, type OperationEvent, type UnitRunResult, type WorkUnit } from \"./operation.js\";\n    10\timport { OperationGit, ensureIntegrationWorktree, type OperationGitPlan } from \"./operation_git.js\";\n    11\timport { REQUIREMENTS_CAPABILITY, READ_OBJECTIVE_CAPABILITY } from \"./objective.js\";\n    12\timport {\n    13\t  credentialFingerprint,\n    14\t  ResourceRegistry,\n    15\t  type ResourceConditionRecord,\n    16\t  type RegistryEvent,\n    17\t  type ResourceDescriptor,\n    18\t} from \"./resources.js\";\n    19\timport { createOperationAccountIdentity } from \"./account_identity.js\";\n    20\timport type { InferenceFailure } from \"./turn.js\";\n    21\timport { OperationRevalidator } from \"./operation_runner_revalidation.js\";\n    22\timport type { OperationDiagnosticHandler } from \"./operation_runner_diagnostics.js\";\n    23\timport type { OperationStore } from \"./operation_runner_persistence.js\";\n    24\t\n    25\texport { OperationStore, OperationLockedError, migrateLegacyAccountIdentities } from \"./operation_runner_persistence.js\";\n    26\texport { AgentWorkUnitExecutor } from \"./operation_runner_execution.js\";\n    27\texport type { AgentExecutorOptions } from \"./operation_runner_execution.js\";\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\texport interface UnitRunContext {\n    31\t  signal?: AbortSignal;\n    32\t  objective: string;\n    33\t  dependencies: Array<{ id: string; title: string; summary: string }>;\n    34\t  /** Why the unit is being resumed on this resource (undefined on its first run). */\n    35\t  resumeReason?: string;\n    36\t  /** Operator decision applied since the unit last ran (told to the unit). `restart` authorizes starting it over. */\n    37\t  operatorDecision?: { label: string; note?: string; restart?: boolean };\n    38\t  /** Durably records the unit's conversation task before execution, so a crash mid-run can be reconciled. */\n    39\t  bindAgentTask(taskId: string): void;\n    40\t  /** Isolated operations: the unit's worktree. Absent means the executor's configured workspace. */\n    24\tconst MAX_EVENTS = 300;\n    25\tconst TERMINAL: WorkUnitStatus[] = [\"COMPLETE\", \"BLOCKED\"];\n    26\t\n    27\tfunction clockTime(ms: number): string {\n    28\t  return new Date(ms).toISOString().slice(11, 16) + \" UTC\";\n    29\t}\n    30\t\n    31\t/** An operator decision Nexus will not apply (stale, not offered, or outside the unit's authority). */\n    32\texport class DecisionRejected extends Error {}\n    33\t\n    34\texport const isRequired = (u: Pick<WorkUnit, \"required\">): boolean => u.required !== false;\n    35\t\n    36\texport class ConvergenceScheduler {\n    37\t  constructor(\n    38\t    readonly state: DurableOperationState,\n    39\t    readonly registry: ResourceRegistry,\n    40\t    private readonly now: () => number,\n    41\t    private readonly onEvent?: (e: OperationEvent) => void,\n    42\t    private readonly onDiagnostic?: OperationDiagnosticHandler,\n    43\t  ) {}\n    44\t\n    90\tconversations); an interactive REPL turn relying on output compacted away in an earlier turn is not flagged.\n    91\t\n    92\t### Decisions\n    93\t\n    94\tA BLOCKED unit carries `{ id: \"<unit>#<n>\", cause, question, options[] }`. Every option is a typed `DecisionAction`:\n    95\t`retry` (optionally clearing operator-needed resource conditions), `keep_waiting`, `assign` (to a named resource,\n    96\tlisting the requirements it overrides — never independence or trust), `revise` (operator note appended to the unit's\n    97\ttask), `drop` (advisory units only) and `cancel_operation`. `ConvergenceScheduler.resolve` validates the decision id,\n    98\tthe option id and the action against current state and throws `DecisionRejected` otherwise; applying one records\n    99\tit on `unit.decisions`, emits `DECISION_APPLIED` and resumes the operation under the driver lock. Operators apply\n   100\tthem with `nexus operation decide <operation> <decision> <option> [--note …] [--no-resume]`. Nothing else mutates a\n   101\tBLOCKED unit.\n   102\t\n   103\t### Rejected decisions\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":859120616}},"started_at_ms":1793205182985,"completed_at_ms":1793205183845}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:33:04.907Z","ordinal":454875,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1835b-a98b-7d22-8934-f8990ce4110b","call_id":"call_12d0c624fa2144749dac1315bbb73464","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5155)\nTotal output lines: 137\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\n\n**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after