 The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 13:34:51 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n\n**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main chec…1655 tokens truncated…ccessful. These source changes are implemented on current `main`.\n\n**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed