{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:33:16.751Z","ordinal":454885,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9916a652-70d0-4164-b219-a414c2e4048d","process_id":"80359","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | sed -n '30,55p'; for f in cli/src/core/capabilities.ts cli/src/core/operation.ts cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts cli/src/core/scheduler.ts; do printf '%s current=' \"$f\"; wc -c < \"$f\"; printf 'origin_main='; git show \"145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08:$f\" | wc -c; done; rg -n 'catch \\{\\}' cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts cli/src/core/operation_runner_diagnostics.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | sed -n '30,55p'; for f in cli/src/core/capabilities.ts cli/src/core/operation.ts cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts cli/src/core/scheduler.ts; do printf '%s current=' \"$f\"; wc -c < \"$f\"; printf 'origin_main='; git show \"145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08:$f\" | wc -c; done; rg -n 'catch \\{\\}' cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts cli/src/core/operation_runner_diagnostics.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"    30\t\n    31\t## Superseded checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 13:34:51 UTC)\n    32\t\n    33\t**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n    34\t\n    35\t**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Requested codebase-review findings:** The prior checkpoint's implementation and evidence summary remains applicable; the current main includes the capability-category split, scheduler extraction, operation-runner decomposition, bounded diagnostics, `DecisionRejected` guidance, lifecycle tests, and 100 fixed-seed scheduler invariants. The operator config remains intentionally limited to `operationPolicy`; general runtime-default customization is not claimed.\n    38\t\n    39\t**Runtime identity dogfooding defect:** The user-reported RC8 behavior in which a Claude-specific skill led the model to describe Nexus as Claude Code has a source fix in merged PR [#273](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/273), integrated at `d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1` (PR merge commit `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`). The fixed system prompt states Nexus Code is the host and is appended after workspace skills; activated skills are also prefaced with `Host application: Nexus Code`. `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` reproduces a Claude model plus Claude-specific skill and verifies both boundaries. That test passed 1/1 in an isolated exact-main `b293b44` snapshot; PR #273's Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed, and exact-main CI also passed. The public RC10 tag (`16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`) predates the PR merge, so this fix still needs verification in the successor RC.\n    40\t\n    41\t**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\n    42\t\n    43\t**Disposition:** Engineering convergence remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. No RC is accepted and no stable release is published. Public RC10 remains the latest release; the repository target is the GitHub installer (npm publication is inapplicable per operator decision). Continue source remediation and exact-head review/CI, then build and qualify a successor RC only after pre-RC gates and PR #305's restart fix pass; keep all installed-RC gates bound to that exact artifact.\n    44\t\n    45\tThe 07:55 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, CI, PR, and qualification state is superseded by this checkpoint.\n    46\t\n    47\t## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 07:55 UTC)\n    48\t\n    49\t**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n    50\t\n    51\t**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.ts` reduced to 12,818 bytes; runner revalidation, execution, and persistence are separated from `operation_runner.ts` (14,931 bytes). Runner decomposition and bounded revalidation/runner diagnostics were integrated through PR [#287](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/287); TDD evidence diagnostics landed through PR [#295](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/295), and scheduler observer diagnostics through PR [#296](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/296). PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297), now merged, adds regression coverage for the TDD diagnostic paths. The capability split and scheduler extraction were integrated through PRs [#286](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/286) and [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285), respectively. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293) added operator guidance for `DecisionRejected` and is merged with its Node 22/24, Linux, and CodeQL checks successful. These source changes are implemented on current `main`.\n    52\t\n    53\t**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\n    54\t\n    55\t**Operator configuration scope:** `~/.config/nexus/config.json` is the operator-owned structured configuration entry point for `operationPolicy`, with schema validation, bounded file size, symlink rejection, and environment/config/default precedence documented in `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`. The schema is intentionally limited to that policy today; this record does not claim every runtime default is configurable or that a repository-level config can override operator policy.\ncli/src/core/capabilities.ts current=10046\norigin_main=10046\ncli/src/core/operation.ts current=14300\norigin_main=14300\ncli/src/core/operation_runner.ts current=21772\norigin_main=21772\ncli/src/core/scheduler.ts current=23696\norigin_main=23696\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":968243312}},"started_at_ms":1793205195782,"completed_at_ms":1793205196751}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:33:18.310Z","ordinal":454886,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1835b-dde6-7553-9726-f0a0a9e18e64","call_id":"call_9d471e03b4654e3799ee22a5c24b7f21","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2769)\nTotal output lines: 34\n\n    30\t\n    31\t## Superseded checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 13:34:51 UTC)\n    32\t\n    33\t**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n    34\t\n    35\t**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Requested codebase-review findings:**…769 tokens truncated…9\t**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n    50\t\n    51\t**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.