{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:39:03.869Z","ordinal":455049,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18361-23bc-7c01-a27f-db665d01e5cc","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed delta `700d16bb1e3b8050f2dbfe91c4c8fd2f89a6ade4..b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b`. Diff SHA-256: `3ec41ef0a83298b70b173a26b2691984b2330fc2abcdbefe27196c4ef2d11779`.\n\nAt [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:364), the synchronous `git rev-parse` probe runs before the code checks whether `config` is a regular file. A nested bare-repo-shaped directory with a FIFO or other special `config` can make Git block while reading it. The later check at lines 382–384 is too late. Also, `--includes` at line 388 permits included config paths to trigger unbounded reads. Reject non-regular config targets before invoking Git and ensure included config reads cannot hang or grow without bound.\n\nThe new tests cover `core.bare=false` and unset, included `core.bare=true`, and preservation of outer index/head and destination canaries on rejection. They do not cover special-file or unbounded include inputs. **Tests were not run**, as requested. `git diff --check` produced no errors."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793205543.8686948}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21786}}
