{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:40:34.014Z","ordinal":455105,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fbd2421a-7559-41ab-be4f-c462ca2aa248","process_id":"33588","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix rev-parse HEAD origin/v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration && sed -n '315,410p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts && rg -n \"include|FIFO|mkfifo|bare repository|core\\.bare\" /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts | tail -60"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix rev-parse HEAD origin/v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration && sed -n '315,410p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts && rg -n \"include|FIFO|mkfifo|bare repository|core\\.bare\" /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts | tail -60"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix\nb9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b\nb9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b\n      if (key.startsWith(\"GIT_\")) delete gitProbeEnv[key];\n    }\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\n      const destination = path.resolve(root, relativePath);\n      const relativeDestination = path.relative(root, destination);\n      if (!relativeDestination || relativeDestination === \"..\" || relativeDestination.startsWith(`..${path.sep}`) || path.isAbsolute(relativeDestination)) {\n        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination path escapes the workspace\");\n      }\n      const relativeParent = path.dirname(relativeDestination);\n      const parentComponents = relativeParent === \".\" ? [] : relativeParent.split(path.sep);\n      const destinationStat = fs.lstatSync(destination, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n      // A directory at the exact destination can itself be a repository, for\n      // example when an untracked checkpoint file was replaced by a bare repo.\n      // Include that leaf only when it is currently a directory; ordinary file\n      // destinations still need only their parents checked.\n      const components = destinationStat?.isDirectory()\n        ? [...parentComponents, path.basename(relativeDestination)]\n        : parentComponents;\n      let parent = root;\n      for (const component of components) {\n        parent = path.join(parent, component);\n        const stat = fs.lstatSync(parent, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        if (!stat) break;\n        if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n          if (allowExternalSymlinkAncestors) {\n            try {\n              const resolvedParent = fs.realpathSync(parent);\n              if (resolvedParent !== root && !resolvedParent.startsWith(root + path.sep)) break;\n            } catch {\n              // Deletion cleanup already skips dangling or inaccessible parents.\n              break;\n            }\n          }\n          throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination parent is a symbolic link\");\n        }\n        if (!stat.isDirectory()) break;\n        const dotGit = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \".git\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareHead = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \"HEAD\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareConfigPath = path.join(parent, \"config\");\n        const bareConfig = fs.lstatSync(bareConfigPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        if (dotGit) {\n          throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination parent is a nested Git repository\");\n        }\n\n        // A bare repository root requires HEAD. The Git probe distinguishes a\n        // real repository from ordinary project folders named `objects`/`refs`.\n        const hasGitDirectoryMarkers = !!bareHead;\n        if (hasGitDirectoryMarkers) {\n          try {\n            const discoveredGitDir = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-C\", parent, \"rev-parse\", \"--absolute-git-dir\"], {\n              cwd: root,\n              encoding: \"utf8\",\n              env: gitProbeEnv,\n              maxBuffer: 1024 * 1024,\n              stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"ignore\"],\n            }).trim();\n            if (fs.realpathSync(discoveredGitDir) === fs.realpathSync(parent)) {\n              throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination parent is a nested Git repository\");\n            }\n          } catch (error) {\n            if (error instanceof Error && error.message === \"Checkpoint destination parent is a nested Git repository\") throw error;\n            if ((error as NodeJS.ErrnoException & { status?: number })?.status !== 128) {\n              throw new Error(\"Checkpoint could not verify nested Git repository state\");\n            }\n          }\n        }\n\n        const bareConfigStat = bareConfig ? fs.statSync(bareConfigPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false }) : undefined;\n        if (hasGitDirectoryMarkers && bareConfigStat?.isFile()) {\n          if (bareConfigStat.size > 1024 * 1024) {\n            throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination has an oversized Git configuration\");\n          }\n          try {\n            const configuredBare = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"config\", \"--file\", bareConfigPath, \"--includes\", \"--type=bool\", \"--get\", \"core.bare\"], {\n              cwd: root,\n              encoding: \"utf8\",\n              env: gitProbeEnv,\n              maxBuffer: 1024 * 1024,\n              stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"ignore\"],\n            }).trim();\n            if (configuredBare === \"true\") {\n              throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination parent is a nested Git repository\");\n            }\n          } catch (error) {\n            const status = (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException & { status?: number })?.status;\n            if (error instanceof Error && error.message === \"Checkpoint destination parent is a nested Git repository\") throw error;\n            if (status !== 1) throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination has an invalid Git configuration\");\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  private assertUntrackedDestinationSafe(relativePaths: string[], targetRoot: string): void {\n    this.assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors(relativePaths, targetRoot);\n    const root = fs.realpathSync(targetRoot);\n1027:test(\"non-Git restore preserves a pre-checkpoint FIFO\", () => {\n1033:    execFileSync(\"mkfifo\", [fifo]);\n1034:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"preserve FIFO\");\n1041:    assert.equal(fs.lstatSync(fifo).isFIFO(), true);\n1074:test(\"non-Git restore refuses a file target containing a FIFO before cleanup\", () => {\n1080:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"FIFO file target obstruction\");\n1083:    execFileSync(\"mkfifo\", [path.join(workspace, \"a\", \"obstruction.fifo\")]);\n1091:    assert.equal(fs.lstatSync(path.join(workspace, \"a\", \"obstruction.fifo\")).isFIFO(), true);\n1200:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses to copy an untracked file into a nested bare repository\", () => {\n1207:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository descendant\");\n1211:    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"config\"), \"[core]\\n\\tfilemode = true\\n[include]\\n\\tpath = bare-core.ini\\n\");\n1213:    assert.equal(execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-C\", bareRepo, \"config\", \"--bool\", \"core.bare\"], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).trim(), \"true\");\n1216:    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"repository-canary.txt\"), \"bare repository canary\\n\");\n1228:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1229:    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"repository-canary.txt\"), \"utf8\"), \"bare repository canary\\n\");\n1241:  test(`Git manifest restore refuses an exact nested Git directory with core.bare=${coreBare}`, () => {\n1247:      const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"bare repository exact destination\");\n1252:        execFileSync(\"git\", [\"--git-dir\", destination, \"config\", \"core.bare\", \"false\"]);\n1254:        execFileSync(\"git\", [\"--git-dir\", destination, \"config\", \"--unset\", \"core.bare\"]);\n1256:      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(destination, \"repository-canary.txt\"), \"bare repository canary\\n\");\n1270:      assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(destination, \"repository-canary.txt\"), \"utf8\"), \"bare repository canary\\n\");\n1280:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with a symlinked config\", () => {\n1288:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository with symlinked config\");\n1295:    assert.equal(execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-C\", bareRepo, \"config\", \"--bool\", \"core.bare\"], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).trim(), \"true\");\n1304:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1311:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with symlinked object storage\", () => {\n1319:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository with symlinked object storage\");\n1325:    assert.equal(execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-C\", bareRepo, \"config\", \"--bool\", \"core.bare\"], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).trim(), \"true\");\n1334:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1341:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with continued core config\", () => {\n1348:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository with continued config\");\n1353:    assert.equal(execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-C\", bareRepo, \"config\", \"--bool\", \"core.bare\"], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).trim(), \"true\");\n1362:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1369:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a partial bare repository whose config declares bare mode\", () => {\n1376:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"partial nested bare repository\");\n1394:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the partial bare repository\");\n1435:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"ordinary directory resembles a bare repository\");\n1635:        execFileSync(\"mkfifo\", [path.join(repo, \"a\", \"obstruction.fifo\")]);\n1650:        assert.equal(fs.lstatSync(path.join(repo, \"a\", \"obstruction.fifo\")).isFIFO(), true);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":76935606}},"started_at_ms":1793205633936,"completed_at_ms":1793205634014}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:40:34.112Z","ordinal":455106,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-757fc2d8-47a7-4e92-8588-21673a2b8b33","process_id":"20567","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '770,825p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '770,825p'","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"   770\t\n   771\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   772\t\n   773\t- Symptom: remote inspection uses the alias or guessed container name. Cause: `ai-5820-01` is not a configured SSH alias and guessed `podman exec` targets fail. Fix: use `mike@10.0.8.5`, then derive container IDs/names from systemd `ExecStart` or `podman ps` under the correct user. [Task 1]\n   774\t- Symptom: remote output includes `Q_PARENT env variable not set`. Cause: command-wrapper noise. Fix: isolate it from command output; do not treat it as host evidence or the SSH failure cause. [Task 1]\n   775\t- Stop rule: the required five reports and final decision portfolio were not produced. Do not claim completion or qualification; continue only within the read-only boundary unless authorization changes. [Task 1]\n   776\t\n   777\t# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n   778\tscope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\n   779\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (worktree used: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10g-rebased); reuse_rule=recheck integration HEAD, claim ownership/staleness, exact CI, acceptance documents, and release state; recorded alpha.2 status and blockers are time-specific.\n   780\t\n   781\t## Task 1: Monitor exact-head CI/reviews and merge PR #10 without calling it a release, success for integration; partial for qualification\n   782\t\n   783\t### rollout_summary_files\n   784\t\n   785\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, PR #10 integrated; qualification blocked)\n   786\t\n   787\t### keywords\n   788\t\n   789\t- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n   790\t\n   791\t## Task 2: Record readiness status while the claim is active, success\n   792\t\n   793\t### rollout_summary_files\n   794\t\n   795\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, held-out payload preserved; readiness files untouched)\n   796\t\n   797\t### keywords\n   798\t\n   799\t- FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md, PLAN-10_READINESS_T2, nexus-claims, stale claim, 24-hour threshold, PR #9, held-out, fresh branch CI\n   800\t\n   801\t## User preferences\n   802\t\n   803\t- reviewers and the release workflow distinguish source/CI acceptance from RC/product qualification -> never call a green CI run a release. [Task 1]\n   804\t- when shared readiness/governance files are claimed, coordinate claim release or wait for the documented stale threshold; do not access held-out payloads or edit the artifact meanwhile. [Task 2]\n   805\t\n   806\t## Reusable knowledge\n   807\t\n   808\t- PR #10 exact head `bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0` passed CI run `39085388798` (contest contract, Node 20/22/24, Linux package/reproducibility) and three independent reviews accepted the code diff. It merged normally to `v1/integration` as `2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2`; the candidate is an ancestor. [Task 1]\n   809\t- At handoff the version remained `0.1.0-alpha.2`; there was no RC, release tag, publication, or qualification run. `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` failed 12 rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-118`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. [Task 1]\n   810\t- Exact-head CI is necessary but insufficient: acceptance requires an installed exact RC, sealed held-out corpus, T2/T3/T4, provider/standalone matrices, human terminal acceptance, package/install/reproducibility checks, and owner-supplied independent RC acceptance. [Task 1]\n   811\t- `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md` requires one worktree per slice, isolated `HOME`, claims for hot/shared files, no `pkill -f`, no concurrent gateway/full-suite runs, and owner-controlled tag/publish actions. [Task 1]\n   812\t- The readiness claims were `FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json` and `PLAN-10_READINESS_T2/owner.json`; at handoff the owner PID was absent but the claim was younger than 24 hours. Resume after release or the documented stale-claim procedure, update against `2c70d39`, and rerun fresh branch CI. [Task 2]\n   813\t\n   814\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   815\t\n   816\t- Symptom: GitHub merge-tool schema validation fails. Cause: `repository_full_name` was omitted. Fix: provide `repository_full_name: \"mikeholownych/nexus-code\"`. [Task 1]\n   817\t- Symptom: PR #9 readiness evidence is canceled/skipped or stale. Cause: it was based on the old integration head. Fix: acquire/release the readiness claim, refresh against current integration, then run fresh CI; never infer qualification from its prior checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":25908}},"started_at_ms":1793205634111,"completed_at_ms":1793205634112}}
