{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:40.941Z","ordinal":455222,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18365-5e0d-7940-81a9-8e7c94f3f3c0","call_id":"call_d991b9fa61af429ab3e68f895767e833","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No held-out status change since the prior review. At `origin/main@ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd` (merge #295, `2026-10-28T03:01:55-04:00`), the T2 and T3 manifest hashes and coverage remain unchanged.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open; last updated `2026-10-27T18:47:09Z`. Its latest comment, #6450709480, is still a coordinator request; no custodian response or handoff is visible. Claims show no active held-out owner.\\n\\nThe T2 report’s historical custody acceptance still separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator continues to reject T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the readiness record remains blocked. No new qualification or fresh acceptance evidence is recorded.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed delta `700d16bb1e3b8050f2dbfe91c4c8fd2f89a6ade4..b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b`. Diff SHA-256: `3ec41ef0a83298b70b173a26b2691984b2330fc2abcdbefe27196c4ef2d11779`.\\n\\nAt [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:364), the synchronous `git rev-parse` probe runs before the code checks whether `config` is a regular file. A nested bare-repo-shaped directory with a FIFO or other special `config` can make Git block while reading it. The later check at lines 382–384 is too late. Also, `--includes` at line 388 permits included config paths to trigger unbounded reads. Reject non-regular config targets before invoking Git and ensure included config reads cannot hang or grow without bound.\\n\\nThe new tests cover `core.bare=false` and unset, included `core.bare=true`, and preservation of outer index/head and destination canaries on rejection. They do not cover special-file or unbounded include inputs. **Tests were not run**, as requested. `git diff --check` produced no errors.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793205820.9414763}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
