{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:58.899Z","ordinal":455235,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2264de8e481a09bc8b42362d6fd09","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’ve replaced Git’s inspection of nested repositories with a fail-closed marker check, so checkpoint restore no longer opens an untrusted nested `config` or follows its include paths. I added deadline-bounded regressions for both a FIFO config and an external FIFO include. TypeScript passes; the checkpoint suite remains under Kimi’s active suite claim, so I’m not running it locally."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793205838007,"completed_at_ms":1793205838899}}
