{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:45:08.463Z","ordinal":455292,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18366-b3ef-76b3-87f7-b1de3a1c161a","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed `35c81484e34b4710d50ce80cc66e7b3aaa8b5ee1` against `b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b`; diff SHA-256: `396f63b3a99da2a0545f6652aca660471891cac71e765a5da2abb6d7ba691570`.\n\nThe FIFO/external-include hang is removed: the new check uses `lstat` on repository markers and no longer asks Git to parse the nested config. However, the replacement heuristic rejects any destination directory containing `HEAD` plus `config`, `objects`, or `refs` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:356)). That rejects an ordinary project directory the existing regression explicitly expects to restore successfully: it creates those four names with a non-bare config and expects `result.success === true` ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1471)).\n\nThis is a concrete compatibility regression. The fix needs a nonblocking way to distinguish bare-repository structure from that ordinary layout, or a different safe policy that preserves the test’s expected behavior. I did not run tests; `git diff --check` was clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793205908.4636526}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21796}}
