{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:52:16.908Z","ordinal":455627,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1836d-3d8c-7653-b4ea-d1f8e9596732","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2774)\nTotal output lines: 110\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...483 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-28 4:52pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (18,980t read) | 138,550t work | 86% savings\n\n### Oct 26, 2026\nS1746 PR #247 RC8 CI monitoring — extended polling loop waiting for Node 22/24 npm test steps to complete (Oct 26, 3:48 AM)\nS1747 PR #247 RC8 CI monitoring — continued polling loop, Node 22/24 npm test step still running (Oct 26, 3:53 AM)\nS1748 PR #247 RC8 CI duration investigation — confirmed normal runtime, not stalled (Oct 26, 3:54 AM)\nS1752 RC10 qualification session resumed — PR #264 review correction, claim reconciliation, and CI monitoring for PRs #263 and #264 (Oct 26, 3:56 AM)\n### Oct 27, 2026\nS1753 RC10 qualification CI monitoring — waiting for PR #263 linux-x86_64 and PR #264 Node 22/24 jobs to complete (Oct 27, 2:30 AM)\nS1755 RC10 CI monitoring — PR #263 linux-x86_64 and PR #264 Node 22/24 still in progress; OpenRouter E5 task classified incomplete (Oct 27, 2:32 AM)\nS1756 RC10 CI monitoring and qualification gate status — PR #263 fully green, PR #264 linux still running, manual terminal matrix 0/15 (Oct 27, 2:37 AM)\nS1772 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — session start status check and PR investigation (Oct 27, 2:54 AM)\n### Oct 28, 2026\n23718 8:51a ✓ Commit 0f04bb58 — Checkpoint Security and Correctness Fixes Committed to PR #302 Branch\n23720 8:52a ✓ PR #302 Force-Pushed with New Head 0f04bb58 Containing All Checkpoint Fixes\n23722 \" ○ PR #302 New CI Started on Head 0f04bb58; Base Now Correctly Reflects main Tip\n23723 8:53a ✓ PR #302 Remediation Update Comment Posted; New CI Run 40659910410 Started\n23724 8:54a ○ PR #301 Operation View Has 3 Open ACTION REQUIRED Items After Two Review Rounds\n23725 \" ○ PR #301 Head Updated to fb193bef Without Review Notification; KimiCode Agent Still Running\n23728 8:55a ○ PR Status Snapshot at Session Start — PRs 299-302 CI and Gate State\n23729 \" ○ PR #299 CI Failure — linux-x86_64 Job Failed on Head bdcfad55\n23730 \" ○ PR #299 linux-x86_64 Failure — smoke-package.sh Exits with Code 13\n23731 \" ○ smoke-package.sh Architecture — Inference Fixture + doctor JSON Schema Validation\n23732 \" ○ PR #299 Claim Owner and Branch State — codex-current-main-rc-path-audit Agent\n23735 8:56a ◆ PR #299 Implementation — Malformed Operator Config Doctor Fix with preAction Guard\n23736 \" ✓ PR #299 Handoff Comment Posted — Requesting Owner Status or Takeover Authorization\n23739 8:57a ○ Issue #1 — Held-Out Evaluation Corpus Qualification Still Blocked\n23741 \" ○ ACCEPTANCE.md Gate Structure — E3 Terminal Matrix and ACC-TUI-MANUAL Requirements\nS1773 Entire Review of PR #301 (operation view) — independent read-only code review while monitoring PR #302 CI (Oct 28, 8:58 AM)\n23745 8:58a ○ PR #300 and PR #301 Comment State — Review Dispositions Confirmed\n23748 9:00a ○ Main Worktree Local Branch — 1369 Behind origin/main, Diverged with Uncommitted Changes\n23749 \" ○ Entire Status — 637 Unpushed Checkpoints, 4 Active Sessions on Main Branch\n23751 \" ○ Active Claims Snapshot — 35 Claims Including PR #302 Ownership and Multiple V1 Defect Branches\n23755 \" ○ Full Open PR List — 8 PRs Open Inclu…305 tokens truncated… safeTerminal Implementation — Two-Stage: redactSecrets then visibleControls\n23779 9:06a ● PR #301 Medium Finding: watch Multi-Op Listing Bypasses safeTerminal on Objective Text\n23780 \" ✓ PR #301 Review Comment Posted — Medium Terminal Injection Finding at operation_cli.ts:237\n23781 \" ○ PR #302 Node 22 Passed; PR #301 Node 22 Also Passed — Only Node 24 and Entire Gates Remain\n23786 9:07a ○ PR Status Snapshot — PRs 301/302 Node 24 Still Running; PR 299 Linux+Entire Failed; PR 300 Entire Failed\n23787 \" ○ ubuntu-desktop Host Not Reachable — E3 Terminal Matrix Cannot Be Started Remotely\n23789 \" ○ ubuntu-desktop Reachable at 10.0.8.3 — All Required Terminal Emulators Present\n23791 \" ○ E3 Manual Terminal Matrix Requirements — 5 Terminals × 3 Sizes = 15 Cells, Safety Checks 2/5/6 Are Gate-Blockers\n23792 \" ○ ubuntu-desktop Desktop Session Active — GNOME Shell Running, All Terminal Versions Confirmed\n23794 9:08a ○ RC10 Installed on ubuntu-desktop at ~/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus\n23795 9:09a ○ ubuntu-desktop GNOME Session Environment — Wayland Only, DBUS at /run/user/1000/bus, No WAYLAND_DISPLAY in SSH\n23797 \" ○ ubuntu-desktop Display Environment Fully Mapped — WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0, DISPLAY=:0, Xauthority at mutter path\n23798 \" ○ X Display :0 Accessible via SSH with mutter Xwayland Auth — E3 GUI Terminal Launch Now Viable\nS1774 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — PR #301 review, ubuntu-desktop E3 preflight, and CI polling (Oct 28, 9:09 AM)\n23803 9:10a ○ PR #301 Prior Review at 08:59 UTC Was ACCEPT; Current Session Added Medium Finding — Two Independent Reviews Now On Record\n23804 \" ◆ Subagent Spawned for Independent Review of PR #302\n23808 9:11a ○ PR #302 Node 24 Test Matrix Completed Successfully — npm test Ran 08:55–09:11 UTC\n23810 \" ○ PR #301 Node 24 Test Matrix Also Completed Successfully — Both PRs Now Fully Green Except Entire Gates\n23821 \" ○ PRs 301/302 Now Have linux-x86_64 CI Jobs Running — New Check Appeared After Node 24 Completed\n\nAccess 139k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem is paused while a provider quota cooldown is active.\n\nMemory capture is paused on claude (five_hour) to preserve your Claude allowance, until 2026-10-28T16:57:35.735Z (5 minutes from now).\n\nReason: Memory capture paused: five-hour Claude usage is 98.0%, at or above the 95% pause threshold. This reserves allowance for interactive work.\n\nThis is not a failure. Incoming observations stay queued in memory and are written\nwhen the cooldown clears — the worker is intentionally not starting the generator\nso interactive work keeps the remaining allowance.\n\nRestarting will NOT help here: it does not replenish the allowance or clear the\npersisted cooldown — so please leave the worker alone.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user that memory capture is paused for a quota cooldown\nat the very start of your first reply. Do NOT restart the worker and do NOT\nsuggest restarting it.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/9b18e506-ad8b-4003-80a5-4ca9502dc3f3.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793206336.9083242,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
