{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:55:31.566Z","ordinal":455798,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18370-35ed-7a40-8c2d-7875d3c6c538","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — this review covers the **uncommitted** diff in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix` against HEAD `934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8`. Diff SHA-256: `d4dc6a43865d2318dcb4c307082a86b465636c36d7d3fa355deba4f989baa7bb`.\n\n`stripGitLineEnding` removes `\\r\\n` as a unit ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:44)), but Git’s path output is LF-terminated. On POSIX, a valid repository root ending in `\\r` therefore loses that character when `gitRoot()` caches it ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:96)). If a sibling exists at the truncated path, path checks can inspect the wrong tree, and restore may target the sibling repository’s index. Strip only the command’s terminating LF and add a regression for a repository path ending in carriage return.\n\nThe other reviewed additions—bounded NUL-path parsing, ignored staged-addition and active-operation guards, and untracked-file mode preservation—showed no further actionable issue. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests; SUITE is held."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793206531.565919}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21812}}
