{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:57:30.576Z","ordinal":455896,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18372-06cf-7300-aeb1-d38239e3d397","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** for the correction atop base `934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8`; diff SHA-256: `38425b0e892f4a0741601516b23ca71a768dc4f08ef06955e6f5869ef47d8527`.\n\n`stripGitLineEnding` now removes only Git’s trailing LF ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:44)), preserving a CR that belongs to the repository path. The regression creates a safe sibling and a CR-suffixed repository containing synthetic sensitive tracked content, then verifies checkpoint creation rejects it ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:67)). This would fail if path parsing redirected the safety check to the sibling.\n\nNo new issue found. The diff is **uncommitted**. I did not run tests; `git diff --check` passed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793206650.5758088}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21815}}
