{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:10:57.843Z","ordinal":456475,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1837e-5833-7621-b283-115526b304f9","call_id":"call_521e4acc8d2d4d1faaece16f831a96a0","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No held-out status change since the prior review. At `origin/main@ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd` (merge #295, `2026-10-28T03:01:55-04:00`), the T2 and T3 manifest hashes and coverage remain unchanged.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open; last updated `2026-10-27T18:47:09Z`. Its latest comment, #6450709480, is still a coordinator request; no custodian response or handoff is visible. Claims show no active held-out owner.\\n\\nThe T2 report’s historical custody acceptance still separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator continues to reject T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the readiness record remains blocked. No new qualification or fresh acceptance evidence is recorded.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed PR #305 head `f0f4847af188f0bf029e018cc8147ddd94a06904` against `origin/main` `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. Diff SHA-256: `05799705a9edccaff8066eaf0287369e7b03863f4d969d754e414a3956b52056`.\\n\\n- **Restart can still resume stale history after an interrupted operation.** In [operation_runner_execution.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts:256), the `recovered?.interrupted` return happens before the new explicit-restart branch at line 274. If an operator chose to restart onto a fresh worktree, but recovery reports an interrupted tool, execution returns only “continue after inspection.” Retrying can then resume the old conversation against the fresh worktree. Honor the explicit restart in this case and preserve an appropriate warning about possible side effects. The new test sets `interrupted: false` ([operation_runner_restart.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/test/operation_runner_restart.test.ts:23)), so it does not cover this path.\\n\\n- **The current-main diff reverts PR #307’s clean-checkout build-identity fix.** It removes `mkdirSync` before writing `dist/build-info.json` and deletes the test that runs the writer with no `dist` directory. Current main has both the directory creation and that regression test. Preserve them when refreshing this PR.\\n\\nNo tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793207457.8434017}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
