{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:11:28.509Z","ordinal":456502,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9a4e413f-a089-42c0-97dd-762f80081fc9","process_id":"56392","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -A45 -B5 '^## 6\\.' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; ps -eo pid,ppid,etime,pcpu,stat,cmd | awk '$2==173625 || $1==173625 || $2==173488 || $1==173488 {print}' | cut -c1-240; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_core_operation_runner_execution.ts/owner.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -A45 -B5 '^## 6\\.' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; ps -eo pid,ppid,etime,pcpu,stat,cmd | awk '$2==173625 || $1==173625 || $2==173488 || $1==173488 {print}' | cut -c1-240; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_core_operation_runner_execution.ts/owner.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"85-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n86-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n87-5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n88-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n89-\n90:## 6. Coordination records\n91-\n92-| Record | Where | Purpose |\n93-|---|---|---|\n94-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n95-| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n96-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n97-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n98-\n99-## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n100-\n101-The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n102-\n103-| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n104-|---|---|\n105-| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n106-| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n107-| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n108-| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n109-| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n110-| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n111-\n112-## 8. Independence constraints\n113-\n114-- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n115-- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n116-- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n 173488  157499       35:49  0.0 Sl   npm test\n 173605  173488       35:48  0.0 S    sh -c node scripts/run_tests.mjs && bash ../scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\n 173625  173607       35:48  0.0 Sl   node /home/mike/nexus-full-all-accepted/cli/node_modules/.bin/tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 test/agent_discovered_verifier_premutation.test.ts test/agent_observer.test.ts test/agent_runtime_identity.t\n 173662  173625       35:48  0.2 Sl   /home/mike/.local/node-v24.11.1-linux-x64/bin/node --require /home/mike/nexus-full-all-accepted/cli/node_modules/tsx/dist/preflight.cjs --import file:///home/mike/nexus-full-all-accepted/cli/node_module\n{\"agent\":\"KimiCode-defect-scan\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/feature-context-management\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-management\",\"base\":\"b2ae2fe8\",\"since\":\"2026-10-28T15:09:42Z\",\"pid\":3822010,\"scope\":\"v1.1 slice 3: per-unit context budget with a preflight decision, durable context checkpoints, view/schema.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":19976509}},"started_at_ms":1793207488488,"completed_at_ms":1793207488509}}
