{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:13:49.142Z","ordinal":456617,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18380-f556-7bc1-9928-103d9c0f6400","call_id":"call_fcbe02b5f11d4402b34f56c25e77c904","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No held-out status change since the prior review. At `origin/main@ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd` (merge #295, `2026-10-28T03:01:55-04:00`), the T2 and T3 manifest hashes and coverage remain unchanged.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open; last updated `2026-10-27T18:47:09Z`. Its latest comment, #6450709480, is still a coordinator request; no custodian response or handoff is visible. Claims show no active held-out owner.\\n\\nThe T2 report’s historical custody acceptance still separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator continues to reject T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the readiness record remains blocked. No new qualification or fresh acceptance evidence is recorded.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for the uncommitted delta atop `cb31461ae5e2d5c5669b86ae670ea0d760757424` (SHA-256 `4f2a1a1c6d2ed574cbcefa9cdf0dc903377d1d44456899ac04a1d9a324f162e3`).\\n\\nThe probe now writes its bounded snapshots through the existing private-file helper ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:491)), and restore preserves a specific, safe nested-repository diagnosis while still refusing mutation ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1239)). No issue found in this delta. `git diff --check` passed; I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793207629.1423085}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_ov