{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:15:27.309Z","ordinal":456707,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-39069bec-2b92-4a7c-adb9-2937bbdbc312","process_id":"50605","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 log --oneline --decorate -8 && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 merge-base HEAD origin/main && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 diff --stat origin/main...HEAD && rg -n '2026-10-28|PR #306|PR #307|PR #302|terminal|held-out|RC10|RC10|source CI|Entire' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -70"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 log --oneline --decorate -8 && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 merge-base HEAD origin/main && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028 diff --stat origin/main...HEAD && rg -n '2026-10-28|PR #306|PR #307|PR #302|terminal|held-out|RC10|RC10|source CI|Entire' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -70"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028...origin/v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028\nd38341f3 (HEAD -> v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028, origin/v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028) docs(release): refresh exact PR qualification status\ndded46ba docs(release): correct RC10 qualification scope\na56432d7 (pr/300) docs(release): refresh readiness at current main\n95912087 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028\n145d464d Merge pull request #299 from mikeholownych/v1/malformed-operator-config-doctor\nc7818480 docs(release): refresh exact-main readiness checkpoint\n11dc196f docs(release): reconcile review timestamp and disposition\n96cc7dcb docs(release): record restart gate failures\n145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 1 file changed, 73 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n235:**RC9 installed accessibility result and source fix:** Published tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` still points to source `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`; its archive SHA-256 is `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. PR [#260](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/260) merged the exact installed-RC PTY evidence as `9def2658e9269f6468ff7c5562839999cc7352a8`; captures and verifier are in [the RC9 accessibility evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md). On installed RC9, `NO_COLOR=1` under xterm at 40x14 and 100x30 emitted no color SGR codes (2/2 subcases passed); `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset emitted reset SGR `39m`, `49m`, and `59m` at both sizes (2/2 subcases failed). The complete all-state accessibility gate remains partial. PR [#261](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/261) now disables Crossterm color output when the TUI resolves `Depth::Mono` and adds a real-backend regression test. This fix is on `main`, not in the immutable RC9 artifact; RC9 remains failed for the `TERM=dumb` subcase. A new immutable RC and affected-gate requalification are required before any stable release.\n239:**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\n256:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; its latest metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Independent private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. Current-candidate provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 is a prior prerelease, not a qualified candidate for this source; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n263:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`. Post-merge CI run [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) is bound to that exact commit: Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. The requirements-enforcement and version synchronization checks previously passed on exact `ff349383`; the version remains `1.0.0-rc.8`. Do not call source CI complete until the Linux job terminates successfully.\n267:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (12:18 UTC). Private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished. No held-out payload was accessed or run. Exact-current-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 remains an older prerelease, not a current-source candidate; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n278:**Terminal environment preparation:** A strict known-host SSH connection to the configured Ubuntu/GNOME desktop succeeded. Read-only inventory found xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; an active GNOME Wayland session is present. This is environment availability only. No manual terminal cell was run, no screenshot was captured, and the §5.3 matrix remains **0/15**. It still requires each of the five terminals at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with approval-panel and post-exit screenshots for every cell and genuine operator verdicts.\n280:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n282:The 13:45 checkpoint below remains as historical evidence; this update supersedes its origin/main, post-merge CI, installed-version, terminal-environment, and current blocker observations.\n290:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open. The latest public metadata-only custody request (12:18 UTC) has no custodian response; do not access held-out payloads or begin the held-out run before independent custody acceptance. The last recorded human terminal matrix is 0/15, with real-terminal operator evidence still required. Exact-current-RC installed qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, T2/T3/T4 qualification and independent exact-RC acceptance are not established. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted but gated on all required acceptance and stable-artifact checks.\n300:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; the custodian has not responded to the metadata-only request, and private custody acceptance, evaluator compatibility and sealing are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Exact-RC provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3 and nine-class T4 qualification, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15; automated PTY checks do not satisfy it. Stable `v1.0.0` is not published. Campaign status remains `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted but gated on acceptance.\n310:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1), for held-out T2/T3 corpus custody, remains OPEN (last observed update 02:33:48 UTC); the required custodian sealing and independent private-custody acceptance are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4 qualification, installed exact-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and the human terminal matrix (0/15 at last evidence) remain incomplete. Treat the older entries below as historical snapshots; they do not supersede these current observations.\n319:**Release state:** RC7 remains the latest public qualification prerelease and does not include PR #243 or subsequent main changes. Held-out qualification, provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4, human terminal evidence, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. Stable v1.0.0 has not been published; publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n331:**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the signature as unverified (`bad_email`); it is not verified-signature provenance. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; both results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n345:**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the signature as unverified (`bad_email`); it is not verified-signature provenance. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; both results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n359:**RC and qualification:** Signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` still resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive digest is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; those results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n373:**Remaining qualification and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public update is the coordinator request from 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no custodian response or new custody acceptance. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone qualification remains incomplete, including OpenRouter; T2/T3/T4 qualification remains incomplete; the five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is unaccepted and no stable `v1.0.0` release is published. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on all required acceptance evidence.\n383:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n385:**Disposition:** Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is not accepted and no stable release is claimed. The next release candidate must include the merged checkpoint fix, pass exact-source CI and qualification gates, and be installed and identified before product qualification. Remaining gates include independent held-out custody and T2, provider/standalone behavior, T3/T4, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted once every required gate passes.\n397:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\n399:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n409:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n411:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\n413:**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n421:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\n423:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n425:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\n435:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n441:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\n451:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\n453:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n457:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\n467:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n477:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release rema