irm && isMutating` with `policy.requiresDecision(cap.effect, context)`. `context` contains the permission mode, source trust, sandbox state and per-origin egress memory. Workspace trust is reported separately and never selects authority.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-108-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-109-When no `onConfirm` handler exists (headless `nexus run`) and a decision is required, the call is DENIED with a typed reason. It is not silently allowed. `nexus run` keeps its current semantics only when `--yes` or `--mode auto` is explicit. The `nexus run --help` text must say so.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-110-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:111:### 5.3 REPL approval\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-112-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-113-In `cli/src/repl.ts:270-276,353,385`:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-114-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-115-1. Before asking, clear the readline line buffer: `rl.write(null, { ctrl: true, name: 'u' })` plus an internal \"typed-ahead discarded\" notice.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-180-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-181-## 11. Dependencies and open decisions\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-182-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-183-- **DEC-01** is resolved as amended: review by default; explicit permission mode controls approvals independently of folder trust. Nothing in this spec is blocked by the decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:184:- **DEC-02** is resolved: the REPL stays a supported secondary surface, so §5.3 is required.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-185-- SPEC-03 provides the trust state for skills and knowledge (`context_inject`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md-186-- SPEC-06 makes the TUI the packaged default, which reduces exposure to the REPL but does not remove it.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-2-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-3-| | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-4-|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-5-| Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-7-| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:8:| Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-9-| Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-10-| Acceptance | ACCEPTANCE.md §4–§7 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-11-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-12-## 1. Problem\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-33-- **EVL-005.** Recovery, intervention and cost metrics are missing.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-34-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-35-`nexus eval` (the SWE-bench-style command) scores the repo's last commit instead of the agent's change, and runs `git checkout` in the operator's workspace (VER-07). It must not be used for any published number.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-36-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:37:Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal coverage (kitty, tmux, VS Code, xterm) is not established. pyte emulation cannot answer kitty keyboard queries (D §6).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-38-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-39-## 2. Requirements\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-40-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-41-1. **REQ-QUAL-101. Held-out matched evaluation.**\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-79-   - Hidden tests are not readable by the agent uid.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-80-   - The scorer logs every replacement.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-81-   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-82-7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-84-9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-85-10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-86-\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md-87-## 3. Design\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":940835881}},"started_at_ms":1793208708805,"completed_at_ms":1793208709747}}
