tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a182df-d9e4-7be3-8ff1-b56ddd57a74a","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_def"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2305f702081a0ab1a1486bcf68feb","order":21851,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1838c-f7d6-7ea2-a58b-bdf86af4e791","text":"The checkpoint candidate now has full independent review accepted on exact base `8580c82`; its clean diff is confined to checkpoint restore code and tests. The old PR #302 head is still failing, and I won’t overwrite its history. I’m opening a replacement branch at the reviewed candidate so required checks can validate it on the current base.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae230cf220481a0967e3335f5142445","order":21852,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1838e-aafa-74e0-9197-4a281c4cea36","text":"The Claude memory observer is unavailable: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.” I won’t restart it. I’ll treat agent review as the available independent review path and continue checking the exact CI and claim state.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae230d8f2f881a091f08be1e21ac448","order":21853,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1838e-d19c-74c0-b6ed-1cf1800483a9","text":"Understood—there isn’t a second human reviewer to recruit. I’ll keep independent agent reviews separate from author self-review, and I’m checking whether exact-head CI has finished before integrating either PR.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2312254e081a0b736e8ccfd178ce0","order":21855,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1838f-ef9f-7b93-93fa-8f19a4bb130d","text":"The exact-main run is still stuck at the full CLI suite on both Node 22 and 24, with no job update since it entered that step; Linux packaging is waiting on those jobs. PRs #300 and #308 also have their own exact-head CI running. I’m checking the live logs and workflow dependencies now, then I’ll act on any actual failure or confirmed stalled runner.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae23155f6ac81a0a72d6e344109b5a4","order":21856,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18390-bad0-7e33-80be-9685c8be3480","text":"The refreshed snapshot still shows source CI running on exact main `8580c82`, and the two PRs are progressing through their own checks. The user-account approval service cannot supply an independent reviewer, so I’m verifying which checks are actually required by repository protection and will rely on the recorded agent reviews for code review.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae231d50d0481a0962b8cf9f5d03f1e","order":21858,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18392-aaf6-7da3-b181-81f6ed2b818b","text":"The safe isolated checkpoint tests have produced a concrete defect on the rebased candidate: several restore cases still fail, including one path rejected by the new staged-addition guard. I’m tracing those failures in the existing checkpoint worktree, preserving the suite claim, and will fix the root cause before relying on its CI.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae231f19c0881a0bf859ed54d73e83e","order":21859,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18393-1a89-7b63-8b12-c863b5e484d2","text":"Milestone: exact-main Node 22 and Node 24 suites have passed on `8580c82`. The dependent Linux build/package job has started and is currently installing dependencies. The PR jobs are still running; I’ll wait for the packaging result and each candidate’s full exact-head checks before integrating.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae23359419481a0a5e99eac19062c2d","order":21863,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18398-9774-7071-9bbc-25a8a76a40f8","text":"The focused failures now trace to two distinct issues: legacy test records retained mode metadata from the newer format, and restore was checking ignore rules for entries it intentionally leaves alone when a parent is a symlink or the target is a directory. I corrected the fixtures and the guarded path handling; the six affected cases now pass. I’m running the complete checkpoint restore file before updating the replacement PR.","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":21864,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200