{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:43:41.906Z","ordinal":457981,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae2344d30ec81a097ed4b8274935416","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I reproduced both remaining failures. One is a path-base bug when the workspace is a subdirectory of its Git repository. The other is Git refusing to create a stash when a staged symlink replaces a tracked directory path. I’m fixing the path mapping first, then I’ll add a narrowly guarded checkpoint fallback that only applies when the index and worktree agree."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793209421220,"completed_at_ms":1793209421905}}
