{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:44:31.983Z","ordinal":458029,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1839d-13ee-7363-b8f0-6f6c2a962d22","call_id":"call_a991f00c2a384f4bb506d9cdc37b7d65","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No held-out status change since the prior review. At `origin/main@ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd` (merge #295, `2026-10-28T03:01:55-04:00`), the T2 and T3 manifest hashes and coverage remain unchanged.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open; last updated `2026-10-27T18:47:09Z`. Its latest comment, #6450709480, is still a coordinator request; no custodian response or handoff is visible. Claims show no active held-out owner.\\n\\nThe T2 report’s historical custody acceptance still separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator continues to reject T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the readiness record remains blocked. No new qualification or fresh acceptance evidence is recorded.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed PR #305 at head `fde0b7b98fc1bde15db3bc4a0afbe85e5ccf8d8f` against base `8580c821f57119768db01614d31cd60e8766468b`. Diff SHA-256: `10fb513891f7f98be7c0fe6d89e5bf1b9eb9f6348cf4ca8390a0b5fb5b7e6d83`.\\n\\nAt [operation_runner_execution.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts:316), an explicit restart now clears the recovered conversation even when its history is otherwise usable, while preserving the recorded verification obligation. The new prompt retains the operator’s decision and the unit’s authorized task; the turn runs with `resume: false`. The TDD path also clears stale RED evidence on restart. The regression test checks that prior conversation text is not reused and that the turn is not resumed.\\n\\nNon-blocking documentation note: [operation.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation.ts:57) describes restart as applying when history cannot be recovered; this change also handles a recoverable conversation whose worktree has been recreated.\\n\\nI reviewed the exact diff and ran `git diff --check`. I did not run tests or the full suite.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793209471.9829788}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
