{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:52:39.186Z","ordinal":458343,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae236661f0081a097fb66f361ff1bfe","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The PR #308 failure report is now reconciled with the local candidate: one failing restore guard was path inspection beneath an obstruction, and CI also caught a raw `mkdirSync` use in a persistence module. The current branch has both corrections, and `tsc --noEmit` passes.\n\nThe full-suite run still active is against a sealed earlier snapshot, so I’ll use its result as candidate history only. After it releases the SUITE lane, I’ll run validation on the current candidate and submit that exact diff for the independent agent review."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793209958182,"completed_at_ms":1793209959186}}
