{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:52:49.896Z","ordinal":458358,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a183a4-ace8-7681-b69e-f3df4d7ffae2","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed the uncommitted diff on base `1482d6b315129cd46fac61242c2eb91793ed8fd2`. Diff SHA-256: `081151dae46d4f6de699839977bfa11d6456f419d48fdb1244acaf14d3a6ba8a`.\n\n- **P1: Restore can delete a committed post-checkpoint file that current ignore rules protect.** At [`checkpoint.ts:1298`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1298), the ignored-path preflight now receives only `stagedPathsAddedToHead()`. That excludes additions already committed after the checkpoint. Yet `removalPaths` at line 1302 still includes `postCheckpointAdditions`, and `removeTrackedDeletions` can unlink those paths. For example: create a checkpoint, add and commit `later.cfg`, then commit a `.gitignore` rule for it and restore. The preflight misses `later.cfg`, but cleanup removes it. Pass the full removal/addition set through the ignored-path preflight, and add a regression for a committed post-checkpoint file that becomes ignored.\n\nThe `diff-files --quiet` guard is useful but proves only that Git sees no tracked index-to-worktree differences at that point. It does not prove byte-for-byte equality against the index in the presence of Git flags that hide changes or concurrent edits. The fallback does separately capture eligible untracked paths; describe its guarantee as Git-visible tracked cleanliness, not all physical worktree changes.\n\nI reviewed the exact source and tests and ran `git diff --check`. I did not run tests or the full suite."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793209969.8965948}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21873}}
