{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:54:49.137Z","ordinal":458445,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a183a6-7eb0-7d40-b824-e17ddc4c5366","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for the uncommitted diff on base `1482d6b315129cd46fac61242c2eb91793ed8fd2`; diff SHA-256: `cdd12be3b649c05f9799d874a880da5829dab613f82c64a67e67ff1d7379b729`.\n\nThe ignored-addition finding is resolved: restore now checks the full `postCheckpointAdditions` set before changing the index ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1286)), and the new test commits a file, adds a later ignore rule, and verifies restore preserves the file, rule, and HEAD ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:624)).\n\nOne fallback gap remains. `git diff-files --quiet` at [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:978) does not prove the worktree matches the index when tracked paths have `assume-unchanged` or `skip-worktree` set. In that case, the index-only `write-tree` fallback at lines 984–986 can omit modified worktree contents that a later restore overwrites. Fail closed when those index flags are present, or otherwise verify the relevant worktree state before creating the fallback snapshot.\n\nI did not run tests; `git diff --check` is clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793210089.1368287}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21876}}
