worktree matches the index when tracked paths have `assume-unchanged` or `skip-worktree` set. In that case, the index-only `write-tree` fallback at lines 984–986 can omit modified worktree contents that a later restore overwrites. Fail closed when those index flags are present, or otherwise verify the relevant worktree state before creating the fallback snapshot.\\n\\nI did not run tests; `git diff --check` is clean.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793210195.117974}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
