default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" \\\n  --used-for \"Inspected Nexus checkpoint implementation and Git index safety behavior for checkpoint restore fixes\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Definition-first lookup located checkpoint create and restore methods; focused details still required source inspection. It did not surface the exact Git fallback implementation or tests by itself.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-inspected-nexus-checkpoint-implementation-and-git.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/inspected-nexus-checkpoint-implementation-and-git\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-inspected-nexus-checkpoint-implementation-and-git.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-