{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:58:34.791Z","ordinal":458636,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a183a9-f026-70e3-8500-9f66032de67d","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed the uncommitted diff on base `1482d6b315129cd46fac61242c2eb91793ed8fd2`. Diff SHA-256: `9da0c57ebb31f82a31b87096e8f857bd8c0881899948360fe17830aeb060a93b`.\n\nThe fallback now detects `assume-unchanged` and `skip-worktree` entries before relying on `diff-files --quiet` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:979)). The earlier restore finding is also addressed: preflight covers all post-checkpoint additions, including committed ones, and the new ignored-file regression checks that restore preserves them ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1286), [checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:624)).\n\nThere are two identical new test cases at lines 1006 and 1036. The first expects `/could not verify protected Git state/`, but the implementation throws “Git index uses assume-unchanged or skip-worktree flags…” at [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:989). That assertion will fail; remove the duplicate or update its expected message. I did not run tests; `git diff --check` is clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793210314.790275}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21882}}
