{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:59:03.164Z","ordinal":458662,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a183aa-5efc-71f1-ab46-a2b07b09b84b","call_id":"call_5cbf31a7bec44cb4a38acf018f963ed9","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No held-out status change since the prior review. At `origin/main@ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd` (merge #295, `2026-10-28T03:01:55-04:00`), the T2 and T3 manifest hashes and coverage remain unchanged.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open; last updated `2026-10-27T18:47:09Z`. Its latest comment, #6450709480, is still a coordinator request; no custodian response or handoff is visible. Claims show no active held-out owner.\\n\\nThe T2 report’s historical custody acceptance still separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator continues to reject T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the readiness record remains blocked. No new qualification or fresh acceptance evidence is recorded.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed the uncommitted diff on base `1482d6b315129cd46fac61242c2eb91793ed8fd2`. Diff SHA-256: `9da0c57ebb31f82a31b87096e8f857bd8c0881899948360fe17830aeb060a93b`.\\n\\nThe fallback now detects `assume-unchanged` and `skip-worktree` entries before relying on `diff-files --quiet` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:979)). The earlier restore finding is also addressed: preflight covers all post-checkpoint additions, including committed ones, and the new ignored-file regression checks that restore preserves them ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1286), [checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:624)).\\n\\nThere are two identical new test cases at lines 1006 and 1036. The first expects `/could not verify protected Git state/`, but the implementation throws “Git index uses assume-unchanged or skip-worktree flags…” at [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:989). That assertion will fail; remove the duplicate or update its expected message. I did not run tests; `git diff --check` is clean.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793210343.1641622}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
