{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:29:16.348Z","ordinal":459417,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a183c6-09bb-70f2-947f-f29f0c3a6914","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted diff on base `1482d6b315129cd46fac61242c2eb91793ed8fd2`; diff SHA-256: `8f52b00989c88a4a8cad9fb949d8c8646dcb1b5b49022f93d3d0fb18bc3f3fe2`.\n\nThe index-tree fallback is gone. When `git stash create` fails on the tracked-deletion/worktree-symlink case, checkpoint creation now fails closed; the regression confirms the symlink target and checkpoint-ref state remain unchanged ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1005)).\n\nThe restore preflight still checks all post-checkpoint additions before index or worktree mutation ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1254)), including committed additions later covered by ignore rules. The stdin-based ignore check safely handles glob characters in filenames, with a regression for a literal bracket filename. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests. The diff remains uncommitted."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","create_time":1793212156.3479698}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21925}}
