{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:38:02.313Z","ordinal":459830,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c0ddf478-e53c-41b8-b798-9f1f2da6e057","process_id":"56358","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 3 'independent reviewer|Independent acceptance|reviewer' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | head -100;"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 3 'independent reviewer|Independent acceptance|reviewer' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md","query":"independent reviewer|Independent acceptance|reviewer","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-17-| `visually-accepted` | A human or independent PTY review accepted the rendered behaviour. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-18-| `product-qualified` | Passed the v1 qualification in ACCEPTANCE.md on the RC. **No requirement holds this status today.** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-19-\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:20:Independent acceptance is recorded separately in the \"Indep.\" column: **Y** = an independent review accepted it; **N** = self-assessed only; **—** = not applicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-21-\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-22-### Release classes\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-23-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-150-| REQ-AGT-114 | quickstart promise | Deliverable binding uses path tokens, not basename substrings. | outcome honesty (false VERIFIED) | `tester.ts:488-570` | TEST (ACC-VER-03; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts, test:cli/test/repro_false_verified.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-03 | **B** | VER-04 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-151-| REQ-AGT-115 | Audit | A zero-executed-tests pass is UNVERIFIED (NO_TESTS_EXECUTED) and keeps the obligation. | honesty | `tester.ts:356-430`; `agent.ts:3516-3675,5360-5410` | TEST (ACC-VER-04; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-04 | RR | VER-05 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-152-| REQ-AGT-116 | Audit | One verifier selector. `run_tests` uses the verifier deadline. | consistency | `tester.ts:19-145`; `tools.ts:1119` | TEST (VER-06; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts::\"ACC-VER-05: discoverVerifier and run_tests return no verifier for Makefile with only pytest: or empty workspace\") | tested | ACC-VER-05 | RR | VER-06 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:153:| REQ-AGT-118 | Audit | Conservative token estimation; `/tokenize` used when available. | failure (context overflow) | `tokens.ts`, `client.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (VER-09; test:cli/test/tokens.test.ts; fixture measured on llama.cpp worker b0-live-llama-worker1, limits_version a3c2fcbc2f2b977c). 12/14 corpora within the 1.5x band (max non-floor over-estimate 1.428x, base64); 4 corpora under-estimate within the 0.8x conservative guard (worst 601/748 = 1.245x, whitespace-indented code); the 2 floor-bound exceptions are recorded per DEC-17. **Amended (DEC-17, 2026-10-17):** the ≥1 token/char floor (admission safety) takes precedence over ACC-VER-07's accuracy band for merging scripts (CJK word composition, Hangul syllables); the floor-driven over-estimate (CJK 2.00x, Hangul 1.67x) is preserved as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. Executed: `tokens.test.ts` 3/3 on snapshot `8cf3e82` and post-merge on `f771a3c` (GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS test-evidence record); independent coordinator rerun 3/3 at exact `2c70d39` with independent reviewer **ACCEPT** (docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/independent-review.md, branch v1/review-plan-11-pr-11d-ag118 @ bc9fd2c). Floor-bound accuracy exceptions preserved as recorded evidence; reconciled 2026-10-18. | tested | ACC-VER-07 | RR | VER-09 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-154-| REQ-AGT-119 | DEC-07 | Experimental surfaces are labelled. `nexus eval` never mutates the operator checkout. Reviewer and researcher roles are read-only. | honesty / safety | `index.ts`, `evaluator.ts`, `roles.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (ACC-VER-08; test:cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-08 | RR | VER-07, VER-08, VER-13 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-155-| REQ-AGT-101 | USER_MANUAL; CLIENT_GUIDE (resume) | `run --resume <id>` continues the conversation, objective and id. A bare `--resume` resolves the latest task. | workflow | `agent.ts:5236`; `app.ts:174`; `index.ts:176` | RT (AGT-01; test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-01, ACC-CONT-02 | **B** | AGT-01 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-156-| REQ-AGT-102 | COMPACTION §C (carried) | Durability is decided by an explicit property. Work units commit compactions durably. | data loss | `agent.ts` depth gates | SRC (AGT-02; test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts::\"all source AutonomousAgent construction sites declare durability explicitly\"; test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts::\"ACC-CONT-03: pressure compaction of a work unit survives SIGKILL and restores archived markers\") | tested | ACC-CONT-03 | **B** | AGT-02a | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-160-| REQ-AGT-106 | EVID-004 (carried) | An escaping exception gives a truthful UNHANDLED_ERROR result with the real obligation. Durable-write failures are reported. | honesty / failure | `agent.ts:4254-4995`; `turn.ts:444-460` | TEST (ACC-CONT-06; test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-06 | RR | AGT-08, AGT-14, VER-11 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-161-| REQ-AGT-107 | Audit | Implementer and tester units cannot be COMPLETE with no change. | honesty | `operation_runner.ts:651-663` | SRC (AGT-11; test:cli/test/team_convergence.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-07 | RR | AGT-11, AGT-12 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-162-| REQ-AGT-108 | Audit | No false stagnation when state identity is unknown. | workflow | `execution_tracking.ts` | TEST (ACC-CONT-09; test:cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-09 | RR | AGT-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:163:| REQ-AGT-110 | HIST-09 | Independent acceptance of continuity, compaction and truncation recovery. | qualification | — | DOC (\"pending\") | open | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | RR | HIST-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-09 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-164-| REQ-AGT-111 | EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE §10 | A single step implementation for the main and subagent loops. | maintainability | `agent.ts:5298-5431` | SRC (AGT-05) | open | — | P (v1: document and add `measureAdmission`) | AGT-05 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-165-\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-166-### 3.3 Local inference and providers\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-256-- EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE I3, I4, stale-lock race, corrupt lock.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-257-- `/tdd` phase enforcement (VER-08).\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-258-- `nexus eval` scoring fix (VER-07b–e).\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:259:- Per-role allowlists beyond reviewer and researcher.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-260-- cgroup containment.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-261-- Network-isolated sandbox for generated code.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md-262-- macOS, arm64 and musl builds (DEC-12).\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-13-|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-14-| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-15-| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:16:| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-17-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-18-A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-19-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-29-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-30-The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-31-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-33-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-35-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-39-| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-40-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-41-| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-43-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-44-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-45-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-281-| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-282-| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-283-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-285-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:286:The reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-287-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:288:The reviewer receives:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-289-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-290-- the RC package;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-291-- this file;\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-293-- SPEC-04;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-294-- read access to the evidence directory.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-295-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:296:The reviewer performs:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-297-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-298-1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-299-   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-336-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-337-- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-338-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-341-- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-342-- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":29714}},"started_at_ms":1793212682312,"completed_at_ms":1793212682313}}
