{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:40:05.380Z","ordinal":459862,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","turn_id":"01a18336-b174-72a1-9e58-590be19b8235","last_agent_message":"Understood. We don’t need another repository member to review every change: a separate, non-implementing agent can provide independent review where the acceptance rules allow it. I’ll keep that review distinct from human approval and won’t treat the release as accepted on that basis alone.\n\nFor the checkpoint fix, the agent review accepted the current diff. The focused test passed on a nearby snapshot, but that run’s diff hash does not match the current diff, so I’m not counting it as current evidence. The `SUITE` claim is held by `kimi-main` for an active test run; I’ve requested a safe handoff and will rerun the focused tests once it’s released. PR #308 still has failing checks on its older remote head, so this work is not integrated.\n\nThe manual terminal matrix remains unresolved. I corrected the claims log because the recorded claim that you waived its screenshots wasn’t supported by your messages. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**.","started_at":1793202762,"completed_at":1793212805,"duration_ms":10043243,"time_to_first_token_ms":3664}}
