{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:49:49.585Z","ordinal":460322,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a183d4-6170-70e3-a371-8f089291fdcd","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae243cca30c81a0a6020540a3723d06","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The first Ubuntu run exposed a test-isolation mistake, not a checkpoint defect: I put `TMPDIR` inside the temporary Git repository, so tests that intentionally delete their own `.git` directory fell through to the parent repository. The focused result was 71/77 and invalid for product conclusions. I’ve identified the cause and will rerun the same exact diff with temporary test workspaces outside the repository."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793213388664,"completed_at_ms":1793213389585}}
