{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:00:35.442Z","ordinal":460701,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a183d4-6170-70e3-a371-8f089291fdcd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-629beb1c-a4f0-4218-950b-93e31526734e","process_id":"19977","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 3 'X5|independent acceptance|Entire Gates|approval' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md .github/workflows"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 3 'X5|independent acceptance|Entire Gates|approval' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md .github/workflows","query":"X5|independent acceptance|Entire Gates|approval","path":"DECISIONS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-25-2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-26-3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-27-4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-29-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-30-The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-31-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-43-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-162-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-163-These must pass:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-164-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:165:- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-166-- `tui_diff_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-167-- `tui_maturity_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-168-- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-169-- `tui_multiline_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-170-- `tui_surface_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:171:- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-172-- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-173-- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-174-- new: the package PTY smoke\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-180-| Scenario | Pass condition |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-181-|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-182-| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:183:| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-184-| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-185-| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-186-| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:188:| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-189-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-190-### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-191-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-201-6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-202-7. NO_COLOR.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-203-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-205-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-206-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-207-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-285-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-286-## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-287-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:288:The reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-289-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-290-The reviewer receives:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-291-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-334-- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-335-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-336-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-338-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-339-- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-342-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-343-- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:344:- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-345-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-346-After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-347-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-34-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-35-| A | Review by default: write, exec and egress ask | Safest. More prompts. Changes existing users' habits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-36-| B | Auto with an enforced sandbox by default | Few prompts. bwrap is unavailable on some hosts (WSL, rootless containers), and the Docker fallback is unpinned and networked. Egress is unsolved. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (original choice; amended 2026-10-24)** | Permission mode controls approvals independently of workspace trust. The default is `review`. `--mode auto` permits writes and commands regardless of folder trust and keeps first-use egress approval per origin. `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass confirmation prompts, including egress. | Folder trust is a separate choice for loading project instructions and workspace integrations. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-38-| D | Keep auto | Contradicts REQ-SEC-101; rejected. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-39-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-40-**Rationale.** Folder trust protects project instructions and workspace integrations from being loaded before the operator approves those sources. Tool authority is governed by the operator's permission settings and must not change when a folder is trusted. A configured `auto` mode remains the operator's choice; when no permission mode is configured, Nexus defaults to `review`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-41-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:42:**Amendment (2026-10-24, operator direction).** This supersedes the original trust-derived mode and approval behavior. Trust affects project instruction and integration loading only; it does not select or change tool approval mode. Approval behavior follows the configured permission mode, with `review` as the unconfigured default.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-43-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-44-**Further rules:**\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-45-- Headless `nexus run` with no TTY: decision-required calls are DENIED with a typed reason unless `--yes` is given.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-49-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-50-## DEC-02: Role of the REPL\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-51-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:52:**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-53-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-54-**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-55-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-207-**Option C, part 2: server-kind conformance (REQ-PRV-106 part b).**\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-208-- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-209-- The fixtures run in CI.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:210:- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-211-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-212-**Release statement:**\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-213-- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-246-| X2 | ~~Provide an independent task author~~. **Resolved 2026-10-14 (T2) and 2026-10-18 (T3):** agent authorship authorized and completed for both T2 (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, sha256 `50895b84…`, 40 tasks) and T3 (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, sha256 `85fb9caf…`, 8 tasks), each sealed under root-owned `0700` custody. | DEC-05 | Done |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-247-| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping proxy plus conformance fixtures). Remaining action: none. Optional: approve a CPU-only llama.cpp container on the dev box for the protocol smoke test. | DEC-16 | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-248-| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:| X5 | Independent reviewer for continuity/compaction acceptance and RC acceptance | REQ-AGT-110, ACCEPTANCE §8 | M5/M6 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-250-| X6 | Provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106; judging is over, so the historical erratum check is no longer applicable | DEC-13 | Post-contest |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-251-| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-252-| X8 | Decide whether to clean the 52k test-polluted records in the real `~/.nexus/tasks` (PER-03). Safe to remove: `task-*.json` whose `workspacePath` starts with `/tmp/nexus-app-test-`. | Hygiene | Any time |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":110518725}},"started_at_ms":1793214034328,"completed_at_ms":1793214035439}}
