{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:05:57.011Z","ordinal":460924,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a183e4-a268-7032-b7b1-4c1c8a680095","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-b07c7112-8f46-4d98-a718-e381118f2546","query":"site:entire.com/docs trail approval reviewers Entire Gates approve trail ...","action":{"type":"search","query":null,"queries":["site:entire.com/docs trail approval reviewers Entire Gates approve trail","site:docs.entire.io reviewer approval trail Entire Gates"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search0","snippet":"Image entire trail resume 1009 ... Review each change without losing sight of the whole. ... Gates. ... Approvals Waiting for your approval Approve ...","title":"Trails · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/features/trails"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search1","snippet":"Review Entire trail 164 ... This approval is required by the trail’s Entire Gates check, which reports “No reviewers have approved this trail.”","title":"fix(sem): stabilize declaration sets and preserve AST types · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a0718c-38d5-7b82-aa26-ef2d67e615c9"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search2","snippet":"Review Entire trail 166. ... Entire Gates is blocked only by missing reviewer approval; its CI, findings, and up-to-date gates pass.","title":"test(graph): retain pinned Linux profiler evidence · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a07bf8-43b4-79e1-a764-74369c5b45f5"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search3","snippet":"* `mergeStateStatus` went `UNSTABLE` → `BLOCKED` — that's just checks re-running plus the still-unsatisfied approval gate, not a new problem. ... Other than the missing","title":"Review PR 127: CLI and SCIP Export Fixes · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/2a557a2a-c9ee-425b-99d7-537a8e69f87d?redirected_from=entire.io"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search4","snippet":"When code is pushed to a Trail, Entire triggers review agents to review the commit. ... To make sure the merge doesn’t happen without addressing","title":"The Git Forge for Agent-Human Collaboration · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/blog/the-git-forge-for-agent-human-collaboration"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search5","snippet":"Review is complete; only Windows CI and Entire’s approval gate remain. ... 8ae5b5ddocs(security): define cache relocation boundary Entire-Checkpoint: 2041b5033e67+22/-2 ... I’m recording your approval","title":"Review and Merge Multiple PRs with Cache Fixes · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search6","snippet":"Review Entire trail 156. ... Entire Gates is blocked only by the required human approval.","title":"Review Trail 156 Evaluations and Merge · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a07cc3-f7c9-7a82-ac15-4810e5b0fea6"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search7","snippet":"Review the open trails in the current repository. ... * Approve and merge it yourself if the change is low-risk and all normal gates pass.","title":"Route Safety and Lexical Scope Merges · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a1491d-38d3-7c33-a2a6-595311c2667b"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search8","snippet":"Finally, tell me which low-risk trails you can approve yourself. ... The repaired allocation guard passes and still rejects the original whole-file split. ... I’m","title":"Synchronize Multiple Trails and Refresh Benchmarks · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a1304c-f8bd-78e0-8932-e7da79a54f3b"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search9","snippet":"* Entire Gates is the trail's own review gate on trail #264 — it was blocked on the open finding I resolved a few minutes","title":"Cache Spool, Flow Routing, and Pipeline Batching · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/13a0a641-2bfd-4dba-b7c7-bfcc16c0f5f9"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search10","snippet":"entire trail approve ... They live in `.entire/runners/`; `entire runner setup` (experimental) creates the default set and can tailor its prompts to your repository using","title":"Overview · /gh/entireio/cli · Entire","url":"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli?redirected_from=entire.io"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.com","ref_id":"turn131search11","snippet":"For example, you have an app, where the app, website, and docs each live in their own repo, all inside one Entire project called `cosmo`.","title":"You Can Now Use Appwrite to Run Your Backend on Entire","url":"https://entire.com/blog/you-can-now-use-appwrite-to-run-your-backend-on-entire"}]},"started_at_ms":1793214356048,"completed_at_ms":1793214357011}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:05:58.177Z","ordinal":460925,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a183e7-a2a1-7cd3-96d5-7619bd9e1d51","call_id":"call_6e6c4984428e4d5b81b4523ef3bbec2d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Trails · Entire (https://entire.com/features/trails)\nciteturn131search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Image entire trail resume 1009 ... Review each change without losing sight of the whole. ... Gates. ... Approvals Waiting for your approval Approve ... Retried usage events are counted more than once, so a temporary network failure can overcharge a workspace.\n\n# Take work from idea\nto merge.\n\nBring context, code, and reviews into one place. Connect changes across repositories, follow the sessions behind them, and see what’s needed to ship.\n\nGet started\n\nKeep the context. Start with the goal, decisions, and discussion. Give everyone the same place to understand the work.\n\nConnect the changes. Bring branches and repositories together under one Trail, with the sessions behind each change.\n\nKnow what needs attention. See review findings, checks, and approvals together, so the next step is clear.\n\n## One place for the work.\nFrom idea to merge.\n\nStart with shared context. Connect the changes as you build. Keep decisions, reviews, and progress attached to the work all the way through.\n\n## Full process\n\nFrom idea to implementation. Turn an idea into a Trail, or start from a change on a branch. Keep the goal attached as the work takes shape.\n\nBilling feature Spec\n\nTrack workspace usage and bill monthly. Support plan upgrades with prorated charges, show invoice history in the dashboard, and keep usage totals consistent when requests are retried.\n\nImageentire trail resume 1009\n\nMultiple repositories. One Trail. Connect the interface, API, and everything in between. Review each change without losing sight of the whole.\n\napi\n\nAdd usage-based billing#1009\n\nweb-app\n\nBuild the billing dashboard#511\n\nAdd invoice history#510\n\n## Automated reviews\n\nMonitors. Follow security and intent match as the code evolves. Open a result to see the reasoning behind the score.\n\nView Intent drift monitor details\n\nIntent drift\n\n7%\n\nView Security risk monitor details\n\nSecurity risk\n\nH i g h\n\nGates. Make the conditions for merging explicit. Bring checks, approvals, and findings together so everyone knows what is still needed.\n\n### Waiting on gates\n\nWaiting for required gates to finish.\n\nMerge\n\nApprovals Waiting for your approval Approve\n\nFindings 1 open finding\n\nChecks All checks passed\n\n## Findings\n\nCatch what you missed. Agent reviews surface actionable findings with code locations and context. Inspect, resolve, or dismiss each one before you merge.\n\nHigh severity finding\n\napi/src/billing/record-usage.ts:42 just now\n\nRetried usage events are counted more than once, so a temporary network failure can overcharge a workspace. Deduplicate events by their idempotency key before updating totals, and add a test that replays the same event without changing the invoice amount.\n\n## CI & Plugins\n\nCI, in the same workflow. Bring build and test results into your merge gates. See which checks passed and what needs another look.\n\n### Waiting on gates\n\nWaiting for required gates to finish.\n\nMerge\n\nImageBuildkite 1 check failed\n\nBuild API Passed 1m 24s\n\nUnit tests Passed 42s\n\nBilling tests Failed 18s\n\nRoom for more. Keep your workflow connected as the plugin ecosystem grows. Bring more signals and tools into the work, in one place.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfix(sem): stabilize declaration sets and preserve AST types · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a0718c-38d5-7b82-aa26-ef2d67e615c9)\nciteturn131search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Review Entire trail 164 ... This approval is required by the trail’s Entire Gates check, which reports “No reviewers have approved this trail.”\n\nI updated the trail description to make clear that the published benchmarks predate removal of the mount cache and have not been rerun on the final code. The working tree is clean, and the final local race suite has reported no failures so far.\n\nThe final full race suite passed. Trail 164 has zero open findings, all 23 CI checks pass, and it is up to date with `main`. Reviewer approval is the only remaining gate.\n\nThis approval is required by the trail’s Entire Gates check, which reports “No reviewers have approved this trail.” The fixes and verification are complete; I need your decision before recording approval.\n\nFixed and pushed through `4afea0a4` to trail 164.\n\n  * Zero open findings; all findings resolved.\n  * Full race suite, vet, build, and all 23 CI checks passed.\n  * Branch is up to date; working tree is clean.\n\nAwaiting your approval. Entire Gates requires reviewer approval before the trail is mergeable; your decision is pending above.\n\ne408807fix(sem): refresh mount inventory for every path resolver Entire-Checkpoint: 9c91d575e11c+55/-242\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntest(graph): retain pinned Linux profiler evidence · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a07bf8-43b4-79e1-a764-74369c5b45f5)\nciteturn131search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Review Entire trail 166. ... Entire Gates is blocked only by missing reviewer approval; its CI, findings, and up-to-date gates pass.\n\n# test(graph): retain pinned Linux profiler evidence\n\nCodex·GPT-6-astra·\n\nashtom·1mo ago·5min·2 Checkpoints·28 file changes·+6711·45.2K tokens\n\nReview Entire trail 166. Make sure the branch is mergable and loop until all findings are resolved.\n\nI’ll inspect trail 166, fix any findings, and check merge readiness. After pushing fixes, I’ll wait for a fresh review and repeat until the findings are resolved.\n\nTrail 166 has no recorded findings, and its CI checks pass. GitHub reports no merge conflicts, but Entire Gates is failing. I’ll inspect the gate and review status, then review the worker changes directly.\n\nEntire Gates is blocked only by missing reviewer approval; its CI, findings, and up-to-date gates pass. A local merge simulation against current `main` also succeeds. The code review has found no defect so far, and the focused race tests are running.\n\nReviewed trail 166 / PR #226.\n\n  * No recorded findings or actionable issues found.\n  * Focused race and regression tests passed; hosted CI passes.\n  * Branch merges cleanly with current `main`.\n  * No code changes needed.\n\nRemaining blocker: Entire Gates requires reviewer approval. The branch is conflict-free, but not fully merge-ready until that approval is given.\n\nPush an empty commit to trigger the Entire workers.\n\nI’ll push an empty commit on trail 166’s branch, then check whether the Entire workers start.\n\nPushed empty commit `b2998b17` to trail 166’s branch. Entire registered the new code version; Entire Gates is running and CI is queued. Checkpoint `fc6b8830a0bc` was also pushed.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReview PR 127: CLI and SCIP Export Fixes · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/2a557a2a-c9ee-425b-99d7-537a8e69f87d?redirected_from=entire.io)\nciteturn131search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;   * `mergeStateStatus` went `UNSTABLE` → `BLOCKED` — that's just checks re-running plus the still-unsatisfied approval gate, not a new problem. ... Other than the missing approval, has the Entire Trail any findings? ... (The \"hostile pathname\" string still appears, but that's my new text describing the original reproduction in the review-revision paragraph, which is deliberate history, not a leftover.) ... PR 97 has no trail, so that reviewer has never looked at it — and everything from `cbf9399d` onward is mine.\n\nThat gives the branch Entire Gates and an agent review over the SCIP encoder and my four commits.\n## Final state of PR 126\n\nHead `8315e1f`, branch append-only from `e8ac679` — nothing rewritten, no force-push.\n\nCheck  | Result\n--- | ---\nlint, bm25-adapter  | ✅\nbuild — ubuntu / macos / windows  | ✅\nstatusline — ubuntu / macos  | ✅\ntest — ubuntu / macos / windows  | ✅\nEntire Gates  | ❌ — Approvals only\n\nGates breakdown: Checks ✅, Findings ✅, Up to date ✅, Approvals ❌ (\"No reviewers have approved this trail\"). Zero findings on the trail across every filter — open, resolved, dismissed, stale.\n\nLocal gate at the same tree (`5488821`): gofmt, vet, build, `go test -race ./...` (all 8 packages), focused test at `-count=20`, statusline 151/151 — all green, with red/green proven both directions against current main.\n\n## What I changed on your behalf\n\n  * Pushed `52ebb7f` (merge of main) + `8315e1f` (test fix) to `security/wrap-stderr-termsafe`, fast-forward.\n  * Rewrote the PR description, with a Timeline section explaining what review found and why the test changed.\n  * Rewrote the trail body to match.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Git Forge for Agent-Human Collaboration · Entire (https://entire.com/blog/the-git-forge-for-agent-human-collaboration)\nciteturn131search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: yesterday; When code is pushed to a Trail, Entire triggers review agents to review the commit. ... To make sure the merge doesn’t happen without addressing the agent findings, Gates can be enabled per repo to define what is required before approval.\nIf the Slop score is orange, you can instruct your agent to continue correcting and pushing based on that data until the score turns green. The last 5 runs and the current run are shown for each eval. We believe this is crucial as one-shot loops are often missing a critical issue. Repeating the loops and stabilizing the scores is crucial for the success of agentic coding.\n\nEntire Trails: Review Agent-Written Code With Context\n\nEach project on Entire comes with pre-defined agents for code quality, security, and slop that can be enabled on a per-repo basis. You can configure your own agents via the Entire user interface or as `.json` config in the repo. Under the hood, Entire utilizes Claude Code and Codex with the latest models, running on isolated cloud sandboxes provided by Daytona and E2B.\n\n### 3. Close All Findings, Then Merge\n\nOn every push, agents can also return specific findings and suggested fixes with different severity levels. Open findings are always visible in the Trail, while resolved findings are hidden, but can be retrieved via the menu. This way, you always stay alert on what is still open. A finding can be addressed or dismissed, you guessed it, by agents or human developers. You can also post findings and comments, just like in a pull request.\n\nTo make sure the merge doesn’t happen without addressing the agent findings, Gates can be enabled per repo to define what is required before approval. These also include human approvals and passing CI checks.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReview and Merge Multiple PRs with Cache Fixes · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542)\nciteturn131search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Review is complete; only Windows CI and Entire’s approval gate remain. ... 8ae5b5ddocs(security): define cache relocation boundary Entire-Checkpoint: 2041b5033e67+22/-2 ... I’m recording your approval on Trail #119, waiting for Entire Gates to turn green, then I’ll merge PR #160 using the repository’s established merge method. ... I’ll approve Trail 146, wait for Entire Gates to turn green on the reviewed head, then merge PR #188 using the repository’s established merge method.\nStill unchanged and still within the configured timeout. I’m watching the exact Windows job step and Trail state; neither has produced output indicating a failure.\n\nThe long-running pair has not flipped state; completed evidence remains entirely green and the Trail still has no open finding. I’m staying with it through completion or timeout.\n\nWindows passed, but Entire Gates failed at the final step. I’m pulling the exact Trail result now; I won’t ask for approval until we determine whether this is a new code finding, stale-state mismatch, or gate infrastructure issue and address it.\n\nThe gate failure is expected and non-code: Entire reports “Checks passed,” “Findings passed,” and “Up to date passed”; only “No reviewers have approved this trail” is red. I’m recording that final state in the PR/Trail, then I’ll hand you the four finding dispositions and ask for the approval that unlocks the merge.\n\nPR #153 is ready at `af34a0f3`.\n\n  1. Trailing-comment inheritance — resolved with real TOML parsing.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReview Trail 156 Evaluations and Merge · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a07cc3-f7c9-7a82-ac15-4810e5b0fea6)\nciteturn131search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Review Entire trail 156. ... Entire Gates is blocked only by the required human approval.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoute Safety and Lexical Scope Merges · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a1491d-38d3-7c33-a2a6-595311c2667b)\nciteturn131search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Review the open trails in the current repository. ...   * Approve and merge it yourself if the change is low-risk and all normal gates pass. ... Use native Entire trail links, not GitHub links. ... Trail 229’s required CI is now green, with all seven evaluations passing on the exact final commit. Its only remaining gate is approval. ... Trails 102 and 262 are updated against the merged main; those merges changed no file contents, but their new commits still need fresh CI and evaluations before I hand over the decisions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSynchronize Multiple Trails and Refresh Benchmarks · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/01a1304c-f8bd-78e0-8932-e7da79a54f3b)\nciteturn131search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Finally, tell me which low-risk trails you can approve yourself. ... The repaired allocation guard passes and still rejects the original whole-file split. ... I’m preparing the handoff with exact heads, gate states, and the reasons for manual review, so pending checks are clearly distinguished from approval decisions. ... d1b4235test(stats): document first-event follow-up attribution Entire-Checkpoint: 044f07325ce3+22/-1 ... The review gates now show only CI and approval outstanding; findings are clear. ... <oai-mem-citation> <citation_entries> MEMORY.md:139-149|note=[manual review hold and exact head verification] skills/entire-trail-review-loop/SKILL.md:24-36|note=[conflict resolution and final verification workflow] rollout_summaries/2026-10-12T13-28-33-7jiH-entire_graph_ten_trail_review_approval_readiness.md:25-28|note=[prior conflict composition and separate trail 244] </citation_entries> <rollout_ids> 01a1304c-f8bd-78e0-8932-e7da79a54f3b </rollout_ids> </oai-mem-citation>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCache Spool, Flow Routing, and Pipeline Batching · /gh/entireio/entire-graph · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-graph/session/13a0a641-2bfd-4dba-b7c7-bfcc16c0f5f9)\nciteturn131search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago;   * Entire Gates is the trail's own review gate on trail #264 — it was blocked on the open finding I resolved a few minutes ago, so it should flip on its next evaluation; if it doesn't follow the finding resolution on its own, I'll nudge it once shard 3 is sorted. ... So the earlier \"Entire Gates: fail\" was purely the approvals gate: trail #267 needs one reviewer approval (self-approval is allowed by the repo config). ... That last gate is deliberately a human action, and since the review on this PR was my own review of my own code, I'd rather not self-approve on your behalf without you saying so.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOverview · /gh/entireio/cli · Entire (https://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli?redirected_from=entire.io)\nciteturn131search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;     entire trail approve ... They live in `.entire/runners/`; `entire runner setup` (experimental) creates the default set and can tailor its prompts to your repository using its docs, history, and past findings.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYou Can Now Use Appwrite to Run Your Backend on Entire (https://entire.com/blog/you-can-now-use-appwrite-to-run-your-backend-on-entire)\nciteturn131search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: yesterday; Crawled: today; For example, you have an app, where the app, website, and docs each live in their own repo, all inside one Entire project called `cosmo`. ... Entire holds each merge until the Appwrite check passes and the trail is approved.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a183e4-a268-7032-b7b1-4c1c8a680095","create_time":1793214358.1771657}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
