 (24)\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"steps\":[]},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"steps\":[]},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"]}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"]},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[\"Run npm --prefix cli test\"]}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\n## v1/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix\n{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\u003e - [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --\\u003e 🔍 Trigger review\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e Run configuration\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - **Source mode**: Auto\\n\\u003e - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n\\u003e - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Layers**: defaults\\n\\u003e - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n\\u003e - **Plan**: Advanced\\n\\u003e - **Run ID**: `91d11591-ce23-4c92-8275-5b6c6dd6ee8d`\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:start --\\u003e\\n- [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --\\u003e \\u003cstrong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\"\\u003eAutofix\\u003c/strong\\u003e · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- tips_start --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss\\u0026utm_medium=github\\u0026utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code\\u0026utm_content=308)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e❤️ Share\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A\\u0026url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai\\u0026mini=true\\u0026title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n\\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csub\\u003eComment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- tips_end --\\u003e\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Exact-head review/CI follow-up for pushed head `87b560c7e581fa71cce270474ba40766f372fb04`:\\n\\n- Runs `40735401162` and `40735870389` both failed Node 22/24 checkpoint-restore tests. The current pushed code passes `:(literal)` to `git check-ignore`; a disposable Git 2.43.0 fixture reproduces status 128 because this subcommand rejects pathspec magic. `--literal-pathspecs` is also rejected by `check-ignore`.\\n- The unpushed `./${relativePath}` adjustment avoids the pathspec-magic error, but leaves wildcard characters in filenames (`*`, `?`, `[]`) interpreted as pathspec patterns. The independent reviewer confirms this remains CHANGES_REQUIRED.\\n- A disposable Git 2.43.0 fixture verified that `git check-ignore --no-index -q --stdin -z` with a NUL-terminated pathname evaluates the literal filename correctly. Please use that interface and add a regression for a staged ignored filename containing glob characters.\\n\\nThe SUITE owner is currently running `make test` on an immutable snapshot. Do not overlap it. After the owner releases the claim, validate the corrected candidate on a Git worktree snapshot (the current archive-like snapshot lacks `.git`, and the build-identity test fails for that environmental reason), obtain exact-diff independent review, push the corrected head, and rerun exact-head CI. No Nexus tests were run by the coordinator.\\n\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Current-head remediation update — `41a63b4c` (base `8580c821`)\\n\\n- Corrected Git ignore checks to process NUL-delimited paths with an explicit `./` prefix, preventing pathspec-magic interpretation while preserving filenames containing whitespace and glob characters.\\n- Focused `checkpoint_restore.test.ts`: **77/77 passed** on `ubuntu-desktop` (Node 22.22.1), using an isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR outside the test repository. The exact candidate diff SHA-256 was `67567302dfe26e478fb762d79133219bf3187750dd77f23b54a1441acaa6fe91`.\\n- `npm --prefix cli run build`: **passed** with isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR. `git diff --check`: **passed**.\\n- Independent agent source review: **ACCEPT**, zero findings, on that exact diff hash.\\n- The previous PR checks failed on the older `87b560c7` head, including the pathspec cases fixed here. New checks are now required on `41a63b4c`.\\n\\nThis update does not claim full-suite, exact-RC, held-out, provider, cross-runner, terminal-matrix, or release acceptance.\\n\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"41a63b4cfbd8c2ec40f384de28db4bea0faee49a\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"BLOCKED\",\"reviews\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":578722158}},"started_at_ms":1793215491449,"completed_at_ms":1793215494029}}